    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 566 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 3): Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 552 base... | Veritas II | 371 | 0.6825 | 0.8582 | 0.0666 | 0.4985 | 0.8885 | 0.9532 | 0.5586 | 0.9538 |\n| 562 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 2): Dual-Path + Task-Specific Heads (ID 552 base... | Veritas II | 369 | 0.6935 | 0.8585 | 0.1365 | 0.4910 | 0.8884 | 0.9520 | 0.5618 | 0.9662 |\n| 561 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Re-replication (Multi-seed Run 1): Dual-Path + Task-Specific\
    \ Heads (ID 552 base... | Veritas II | 368 | 0.6770 | 0.8588 | 0.0765 | 0.4620 | 0.8908 | 0.9524 | 0.5540 | 0.9446 |\n| 556 | 1 | Veritas II - SOTA Replication: Dual-Path + Task-Specific Prediction Heads (ID 552) | Veritas II | 366 | 0.6799 | 0.8604 | 0.0845 | 0.4585 | 0.8898 | 0.9525 | 0.5613 | 0.9523 |\n| 552 | 1 | Veritas II - Dual-Path + Task-Specific Prediction Heads | Veritas II | 364 | 0.6835 | 0.8587 | 0.0667 | 0.5015 | 0.8898 | 0.9528 | 0.5578 | 0.9569 |\n| 546 | 1 | Veritas II - Dual-Path Ablation: Targeted Dropout in Conv-Motif Detector (0.05) | Veritas II | 360 | 0.6804 | 0.8583 | 0.0447 | 0.5063 | 0.8915 | 0.9531 | 0.5687 | 0.9400 |\n| 541 | 1 | Veritas II - Dual-Path Ablation: Deeper (2-Layer) Conv-Motif Detector (Kernel 5, Narrowed) | Veritas II | 357 | 0.6755 | 0.8608 | 0.0150 | 0.4860 | 0.8981 | 0.9530 | 0.5693 | 0.9462 |\n| 515 | 1 | Veritas II - Dual-Path: Conv-Motif Detector (Kernel 5) Re-run for Reproducibility | Veritas II | 344 | 0.6828 | 0.8597 | 0.0695 | 0.4895\
    \ | 0.8967 | 0.9522 | 0.5615 | 0.9508 |\n| 512 | 1 | Veritas II - Dual-Path Ablation: Conv-Motif Detector (Kernel 3) | Veritas II | 342 | 0.6781 | 0.8595 | 0.0322 | 0.5004 | 0.8866 | 0.9519 | 0.5685 | 0.9477 |\n| 508 | 1 | Veritas II - Dual-Path: DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector (Kernel 5) | Veritas II | 340 | 0.6812 | 0.8564 | 0.0567 | 0.4882 | 0.8924 | 0.9520 | 0.5658 | 0.9569 |\n\nPage 1 of 10 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-10, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/veritas/utils.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# Depthwise Separable Dilated Convolutional Block (GELU activations)\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    dilation: int = 1\n\
    \    dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(\n            features=self.d_model,\n            kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n            feature_group_count=self.d_model, # Depthwise\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n            name='dw_conv'\n        )(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h) # GELU activation\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\nclass DSConvNetworkWrapper: # Generic wrapper for DSConv-based networks\n    def __init__(self, model_instance): \n        self.network = model_instance\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key, 2) # Split for params and dropout\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout':\
    \ dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if rng_key is None:\n            rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
