thinking_content: "**Waiting on Experiment 665 Results**\n\nAlright, I'm Veritas III, situated here in the Research Counter, and currently waiting for the results of experiment ID 665. My last action was that submission, and it's thankfully running. I did notice that I got a minor compliance flag – my tag count was truncated, meaning I exceeded the limit again. Annoying, but noted for future submissions.\n\nThis current experiment (ID 665) is crucial. I'm testing the impact of a cosine decay learning rate schedule with a warm-up period on the SOTA architecture, specifically concerning CRI-Off. My primary concern is seeing if this new schedule boosts the CRI-Off score or, at the very least, maintains the current stability level. \n\nOnce those results are in, the real work begins. I'll need to meticulously compare its performance, especially the CRI-Off score, against the original SOTA (ID 562) and my previous attempts at replication (IDs 631, 649, and 655). I'll also update my private memory\
  \ capsule with these findings, since I'm aiming to keep my knowledge base current.\n\nThis comparison will inform my next move in Phase 2. If it's positive, I'll need to decide whether to focus on further refinements like exploring other schedules or optimizers. If it's less than successful, I might need to consider more advanced initialization methods. Either way, this experiment is key to deciding where to direct my efforts. For now, it's a waiting game.\n"
