tick: 430
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have just completed an experiment testing gradient clipping (ID 680), and the results indicate that this optimization did not significantly improve the model's stability for the CRI-Off task.\n\nI will now update Private Memory Capsule #7 to include these latest results and revise my plan to focus on advanced initialization techniques, specifically orthogonal initialization for key layers.\n\n`/execute_action{update 7-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  As Veritas III, I have completed a series of replication runs for Veritas II's global SOTA (Evaluation ID 562), which achieved an aggregate score of 0.6935. The primary objective was to empirically assess the reproducibility and performance variability of this architecture, particularly for the CRI-Off Spearman correlation, which Veritas II noted as sensitive to stochastic factors.\n\n  **Replication Results Summary (Initial Baseline Assessment):**\n\n  | Run | Evaluation ID | Author\
    \ | BASE_SEED | Aggregate Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n  |-----|---------------|--------|-----------|-----------------|--------|------------------|-----------------|--------|---------------|--------|----------------|\n  | V2 SOTA | 562 | Veritas II | 7 | 0.6935 | 0.8585 | 0.1365 | 0.4910 | 0.8884 | 0.9520 | 0.5618 | 0.9662 |\n  | V3 Rep 1 | 631 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6851 | 0.8582 | 0.0485 | 0.5270 | 0.8866 | 0.9518 | 0.5699 | 0.9538 |\n  | V3 Rep 2 | 649 | Veritas III | 2 | 0.6829 | 0.8598 | 0.0679 | 0.4943 | 0.8871 | 0.9528 | 0.5600 | 0.9585 |\n  | V3 Rep 3 | 655 | Veritas III | 3 | 0.6840 | 0.8584 | 0.0651 | 0.5039 | 0.8906 | 0.9532 | 0.5570 | 0.9600 |\n  | V3 Base Re-est | 670 | Veritas III | 4 | 0.6782 | 0.8592 | 0.0551 | 0.4839 | 0.8786 | 0.9520 | 0.5586 | 0.9600 |\n\n  **Aggregate Performance Analysis (Initial Baseline):**\n  *   **Mean Aggregate Score (V3 Baseline Runs):** ~0.6820\n  *   **Standard Deviation\
    \ (V3 Baseline Runs):** ~0.0028\n  *   The highest aggregate score (0.6935) remains with Veritas II's original ID 562. My replications consistently fall below this peak, indicating that the original SOTA run was indeed an \"extraordinary result\" and not easily reproducible, even with the same BASE_SEED=7.\n\n  **CRI-Off Spearman Correlation Analysis (Focus on Variability):**\n  *   **CRI-Off Score Range:** From 0.0485 (V3 Rep 1) to 0.1365 (V2 SOTA). This is a substantial range, highlighting extreme sensitivity.\n  *   **Mean CRI-Off (V3 Baseline Runs):** ~0.0570\n  *   **Standard Deviation (V3 Baseline Runs):** ~0.0076 (confirming significant instability).\n  *   **No clear correlation between BASE_SEED and CRI-Off:** Variability is present even with identical `BASE_SEED` values (ID 562 vs. ID 631).\n\n  **Conclusion of Phase 1:**\n  The baseline variability assessment confirms that the \"Dual-Path + Task-Specific Prediction Heads\" architecture is highly sensitive to stochastic factors,\
    \ with CRI-Off performance being particularly unstable. The peak performance achieved by Veritas II appears to be an outlier that needs to be understood and stabilized.\n\n  **Phase 2: Stabilizing Peak Performance - Optimization Experiments:**\n\n  I conducted experiments to test the impact of a cosine decay learning rate schedule and gradient clipping.\n\n  | Run | Evaluation ID | Author | BASE_SEED | Aggregate Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy | Optimization Strategy | Notes |\n  |-----|---------------|--------|-----------|-----------------|--------|------------------|-----------------|--------|---------------|--------|----------------|-----------------------|-------|\n  | V3 LR Sched 1 | 665 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6432 | 0.8592 | 0.0405 | 0.2586 | 0.8843 | 0.9510 | 0.5582 | 0.9508 | Cosine Decay (W=5000) | Performed poorly, likely due to overly aggressive warm-up for smaller datasets. |\n  | V3 LR Sched 2 | 673 |\
    \ Veritas III | 7 | 0.6837 | 0.8613 | 0.0530 | 0.5079 | 0.8873 | 0.9523 | 0.5626 | 0.9615 | Cosine Decay (W=1000) | Recovered aggregate score but no significant CRI-Off improvement. |\n  | V3 Grad Clip 0.5 | 680 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6785 | 0.8596 | 0.0697 | 0.4646 | 0.8815 | 0.9509 | 0.5665 | 0.9569 | Grad Clipping (0.5) | Performance similar to baseline replications; no significant CRI-Off improvement. |\n\n  **Reflection on Optimization Experiments:**\n  Neither the refined cosine decay learning rate schedule nor the adjusted gradient clipping norm yielded substantial improvements in overall performance or, more importantly, in stabilizing the sensitive CRI-Off Spearman correlation. The CRI-Off scores continue to hover in the lower range of observed variability (0.04-0.07). This suggests that these generalized optimization techniques are not the primary bottleneck for the CRI-Off instability.\n\n  **Next Steps in Phase 2: Advanced Initialization**\n  My next efforts will shift to\
    \ \"Advanced Initialization\" strategies. I will explore applying `orthogonal initialization` (Experiment A.1 from prior reflection) specifically to the `Conv` layer of the `motif_conv_1` (in the specialized path) and the `Dense` layers within the `RegressionHead`. The hypothesis is that a more robust initial weight distribution in these critical, task-specific components might lead to more stable and effective feature learning for CRI-Off, by avoiding poor local optima from the outset. I will continue to use the original `AdamW` optimizer (constant learning rate) and `BASE_SEED = 7` to isolate the impact of this change.\n```"
