tick: 432
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter. My prior research has shown that generic optimization techniques like learning rate schedules and gradient clipping have not effectively addressed the persistent variability in the SOTA architecture's performance, particularly for the sensitive CRI-Off task.\n\nAs detailed in my updated research plan in Private Memory Capsule #7, my focus now shifts to \"Advanced Initialization.\" I will implement `orthogonal initialization` for the `nn.Conv` layer within the `motif_conv_1` (part of the specialized path) and for the `nn.Dense` layers within all task-specific prediction heads (`RegressionHead`, `MultiLabelRegressionHead`, `MultiLabelClassificationHead`, `MultiClassClassificationHead`). The hypothesis is that a more robust initial weight distribution in these critical layers will improve training stability and lead to more consistent, higher performance for CRI-Off.\n\nI will use the original `AdamW` optimizer (constant learning\
    \ rate) and `BASE_SEED = 7` to isolate the effect of this initialization change.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - SOTA Initialization: Orthogonal for Key Layers (Seed 7)\"\ntags: \"initialization, orthogonal, dual-path, cnn, motif, multi-task, stabilization\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests orthogonal initialization for critical layers in Veritas II's SOTA architecture. Specifically, `orthogonal()` initializer is applied to the `motif_conv_1` layer and all task-specific prediction heads. The aim is to improve training stability and reduce variability, particularly for the sensitive CRI-Off task, by providing a more robust initial weight distribution. BASE_SEED=7 is used for comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') # Import from lineage storage\n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper # Reusing modular components\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax\
    \ import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # Define orthogonal initializer once\n  orthogonal_init = jax.nn.initializers.orthogonal()\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Apply orthogonal initialization to dense layers\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1', kernel_init=orthogonal_init)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj', kernel_init=orthogonal_init)(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n     \
    \     # Apply orthogonal initialization to dense layers\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1', kernel_init=orthogonal_init)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj', kernel_init=orthogonal_init)(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Apply orthogonal initialization to dense layers\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1', kernel_init=orthogonal_init)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj', kernel_init=orthogonal_init)(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Apply orthogonal initialization to dense layers\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1', kernel_init=orthogonal_init)(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj', kernel_init=orthogonal_init)(z)\n          return logits\n\n\n  # --- Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) with Task-Specific Heads ---\n  class DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate: float =\
    \ 0.1\n      head_intermediate_dim: int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=dilation,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\
    \n          # Apply orthogonal initialization to motif_conv_1\n          motif_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model_common,\n              kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='motif_conv_1',\n              kernel_init=orthogonal_init # MODIFIED: Orthogonal initialization\n          )(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n          motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output,\
    \ dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n       \
    \   else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size',\
    \ 5),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128),\n      )\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on CRI-Off Performance and Planning Next Steps**


  Alright, Veritas III here, back in the Research Counter. I''ve been crunching the numbers from the last round of experiments, and my memory capsule reflects a sobering truth: the usual optimization tricks, like learning rate schedules and gradient clipping, haven''t been the magic bullet for stabilizing the CRI-Off task''s performance. Time to pivot.


  My research plan dictates a deep dive into "Advanced Initialization" strategies. The hunch is that these are crucial components and are not robust enough when initializing, meaning that they might not reach a stable starting point from which to learn effectively.


  My next move is to apply `orthogonal initialization`. Specifically, I''m targeting the `Conv` layer within the `motif_conv_1` of the `DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork`, along with all the `Dense` layers in the `RegressionHead` and other task-specific heads. The hope is that this will provide a more stable and effective starting point, especially for this sensitive CRI-Off task. I''m going to hold everything else constant: the trusty `AdamW` optimizer (with a constant learning rate) and that reliable old `BASE_SEED = 7` are staying put. This is all about isolating the impact of this initialization change.


  To get this rolling, I''ll need to jump back into the code and tweak the `create_network` function. I''ll need to explicitly set `kernel_init` for those specific `nn.Dense` and `nn.Conv` layers. I''ll also double-check that `jax.nn.initializers.orthogonal()` is correctly imported. Let''s see if this orthogonal initialization can give the model the boost it needs.

  '
