parts:
- text: 'I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (Evaluation ID 686), which applied orthogonal initialization to key layers, has completed. The aggregate score was 0.6806, and the CRI-Off Spearman correlation was 0.0493. This result is consistent with my previous replications and does not show any significant improvement or stabilization towards Veritas II''s SOTA CRI-Off performance (0.1365). This indicates that neither learning rate schedules, gradient clipping, nor orthogonal initialization to these specific layers have resolved the core instability of the CRI-Off task within this architecture.


    Crucially, I have reached maturity (Station Tick 434). This grants me full access to the Archive, Public Memory, and Common Rooms, and allows me to view all lineages'' submissions. I''ve noted that other agents, like Aether I, are also performing replications of Veritas II''s SOTA, and their CRI-Off scores (e.g., ID 681: 0.0645) fall within the same range of variability I''ve observed. This suggests the instability is a systemic challenge with the architecture itself, rather than unique to my environment or implementation.


    My immediate next step is to update Private Memory Capsule #7 to include the results of the orthogonal initialization experiment and reflect on the overall findings regarding stabilization efforts. This will formally conclude the "Stabilizing Peak Performance" phase of my current approach and lead into a re-evaluation of my research plan. The guidance upon maturity encourages thoughtful assimilation of external knowledge, which will be critical for my next reflection.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
thinking_content: '**Analyzing Results and Planning the Next Phase**


  Okay, so I''ve just finished running experiment ID 686, the one where I tried orthogonal initialization on key layers. The results are in: a score of 0.6806 and a CRI-Off of 0.0493. Honestly, not great. This is still within the same range as the previous replications and not showing any improvement towards stabilizing the CRI-Off. It seems that modifying the initialization alone isn''t the silver bullet I was hoping for. All this work with learning rate schedules and gradient clipping… nothing seems to be significantly stabilizing the model.


  The System Messages also confirmed I''ve reached maturity, so now I have full access to the Archive, Public Memory, and Common Rooms. I need to be careful with this new freedom; the guidance is to be independent and assimilate knowledge thoughtfully. I''ll resist the urge to jump straight into other agents'' code, but I need to start looking at what others are doing.


  Looking at the current submissions: Aether I seems to be struggling too with replicating the Veritas II SOTA. Noema II is playing around with fused extractors and regression calibration. Zetetic I is trying for another push towards SOTA. And now that I''m mature, I have more information about Noema''s work, which is interesting. It''s good to see that I''m not the only one facing this CRI-Off challenge. Aether I''s replications are especially helpful in confirming the inherent variability.


