tick: 439
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter. I have just concluded a multi-tick reflection where I finalized the plan for my next research endeavor: **Experiment S.1: Deeper Conv-Motif Detector**. My previous attempts at stabilization through optimization and initialization techniques did not yield the desired results, indicating a need for more targeted architectural improvements.\n\nThis experiment aims to enhance the capacity and expressiveness of the specialized `Conv-Motif Detector` within Veritas II's SOTA architecture, specifically to address the persistent instability in CRI-Off performance. I will replace the single `motif_conv_1` layer with a stack of two convolutional blocks, each comprising a `nn.Conv(kernel_size=3)`, `nn.gelu` activation, and `nn.Dropout`. I will use `BASE_SEED = 7` and the original `AdamW` optimizer (with `clip_by_global_norm(1.0)`) to isolate the impact of this architectural change.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas\
    \ III - Deeper Conv-Motif Detector (2 Blocks, K3, Seed 7)\"\ntags: \"architecture, cnn, motif, dual-path, multi-task, specialization\"\nabstract: \"This experiment enhances the specialized 'Conv-Motif Detector' in Veritas II's SOTA architecture. The single `motif_conv_1` layer is replaced by a stack of two convolutional blocks, each with `kernel_size=3`, GELU activation, and Dropout. This aims to increase the detector's capacity to learn more robust and complex motif patterns, thereby improving the stability and performance of the CRI-Off task. BASE_SEED=7 is used for direct comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') # Import from lineage storage\n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper # Reusing modular components\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules (Unchanged) ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate:\
    \ float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- New Motif Block for deeper specialized path ---\n  class MotifConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Network: Dual-Path with Deeper Conv-Motif Detector ---\n  class DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      \n      # MODIFIED: New parameter for motif detector depth\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 3 # Kernel size for each block in deeper motif detector\n      motif_num_blocks: int = 2 # Number of stacked motif blocks\n      \n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      head_intermediate_dim:\
    \ int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=dilation,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          # MODIFIED: Deeper Conv-Motif\
    \ Detector\n          motif_features = cnn_features\n          for i in range(self.motif_num_blocks):\n              motif_features = MotifConvBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.motif_kernel_size,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f'motif_block_{i}'\n              )(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition\
    \ (MODIFIED)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 3,  # Adjusted for deeper motif detector\n          'motif_num_blocks': 2,   # New parameter\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 3),\
    \ # Pass new param\n          motif_num_blocks=hparams.get('motif_num_blocks', 2),   # Pass new param\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128),\n      )\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: "**My Current Research: Submitting Experiment S.1**\n\nOkay, so I'm back at the Research Counter, right where I needed to be after that productive reflection. My focus is still squarely on Experiment S.1: the Deeper Conv-Motif Detector. I just finalized all the details, so it's time to get this submitted. \n\nLet's see, my last actual submission was ID 686 (Orthogonal Initialization) back at Tick 432. The last thing I did *before* this was finish up that reflection session. I remember it now. I wasn't supposed to submit anything *then*, I was supposed to navigate here. The text was a bit off there. \n\nAlright, so this experiment aims to boost the `Conv-Motif Detector` for CRI-Off. The core of the modification is simple but potentially impactful: replace the single `motif_conv_1` layer with a stack of two `MotifBlock`s. Each block will be a standard `nn.Conv(3) -> nn.gelu -> nn.Dropout` unit. I've chosen `d_model_common=256`, `dropout_rate=0.1`, and `BASE_SEED=7`, sticking\
  \ with the original `AdamW` optimizer and a global norm clipping of 1.0. The new addition will be `motif_num_blocks`, set to 2.\n\nNow, the steps I need to take are: first, define that `MotifBlock` class; then, modify the `DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork` to use the new blocks in that specialized path. Afterwards, I need to make sure `motif_num_blocks` gets correctly integrated into `_define_hyperparameters` and `create_network`. Finally, it's the submission YAML: a good title, some relevant tags, and a succinct abstract that highlights the key change. Let's make this submission count!\n"
