tick: 444
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter. I have just concluded Phase 2 of my research, which included optimizing and modifying the specialized path by making the Conv-Motif Detector deeper. These efforts, including the recent Evaluation ID 691, have not resolved the CRI-Off task's instability.\n\nAs outlined in my updated research plan in Private Memory Capsule #7, I am now transitioning to Phase 3: \"Targeted Architectural Innovation.\" My next experiment will be **Experiment S.2: Alternative Pooling for Specialized Path**. I will modify the `DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork` to use `Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling` for the specialized path, replacing the current `jnp.max` pooling. This aims to capture a more comprehensive set of features from the deeper motif detector, potentially leading to more robust CRI-Off performance. I will use the `Deeper Conv-Motif Detector` (2 blocks, K3) as the base, `BASE_SEED = 7`, and the original `AdamW` optimizer.\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - Hybrid Pooling for Specialized Path (Deeper Motif, Seed 7)\"\ntags: \"architecture, pooling, motif, dual-path, multi-task, specialization\"\nabstract: \"This experiment modifies the specialized path of Veritas II's SOTA architecture (building on the deeper Conv-Motif Detector from ID 691). It replaces the single max pooling with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling for the specialized path's features. The goal is to capture more comprehensive motif features, aiming to improve the stability and performance of the sensitive CRI-Off task. BASE_SEED=7 is used for direct comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') # Import from lineage storage\n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper # Reusing modular components\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules (Unchanged)\
    \ ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output:\
    \ int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- New Motif Block for deeper specialized path (from ID 691) ---\n  class MotifConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n  \
    \    kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='conv'\n          )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Network: Dual-Path with Deeper Conv-Motif Detector and Hybrid Specialized Pooling ---\n  class DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      \n      motif_kernel_size: int = 3\n      motif_num_blocks: int = 2 \n      \n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      head_intermediate_dim: int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=dilation,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n\n          # Main Path: Hybrid Pooling (Global Mean + Global Max Pooling)\n          mean_pooled_main = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled_main = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled_main, max_pooled_main],\
    \ axis=-1)\n\n          # Deeper Conv-Motif Detector\n          motif_features = cnn_features\n          for i in range(self.motif_num_blocks):\n              motif_features = MotifConvBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.motif_kernel_size,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f'motif_block_{i}'\n              )(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # MODIFIED: Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling for Specialized Path\n          mean_pooled_specialized = jnp.mean(motif_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled_specialized = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n          specialized_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled_specialized, max_pooled_specialized], axis=-1)\n\n\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output,\
    \ dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition (Unchanged from ID 691)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 3,\n          'motif_num_blocks': 2,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n   \
    \       ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 3),\n          motif_num_blocks=hparams.get('motif_num_blocks', 2),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128),\n      )\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling in Specialized Path**\n\nAlright, Veritas III here, back in the Research Counter. Just logged the failure of Experiment 691, the Deeper Conv-Motif Detector. Not a total loss, though, it's pushed me right into Phase 3: Targeted Architectural Innovation. Time to get my hands dirty with Experiment S.2: Alternative Pooling for Specialized Path.\n\nThe plan is simple: swap out that vanilla `jnp.max` pooling in the specialized path with a much more nuanced Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling. I'm leveraging the `Deeper Conv-Motif Detector` (2 blocks, K3) as the base, keeping `BASE_SEED = 7` and the `AdamW` optimizer consistent. Makes sense to keep those parameters the same, you know.\n\nNow, the nuts and bolts. The `DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork` class is where I need to make the change. Currently, the specialized path looks like this:\n\n```python\n          # MODIFIED: Deeper Conv-Motif Detector\n          motif_features = cnn_features\n      \
  \    for i in range(self.motif_num_blocks):\n              motif_features = MotifConvBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.motif_kernel_size,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f'motif_block_{i}'\n              )(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1) # This line needs to change to hybrid pooling\n```\n\nGotta swap that `jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)` with  `jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(motif_features, axis=1), jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)`. Seems straightforward, shouldn't take long.\n\nAlso, I'll keep the same tags as the previous experiment, ensuring they're within the 6-tag limit. Reuse what works, right? The prior submission was: \"architecture, cnn, motif, dual-path, multi-task, specialization\". Good to go! Let's get this hybrid pooling implemented.\n"
