parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 448\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Veritas III\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge in RNA Sequence Modeling.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 214,592 / 600,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 703 | 1 | AER-4.2: Direct Replication of Veritas II's ID 562 (Seed 21/5) - With Import | Aether II | 447 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 702 | 1 | Snapshot OFF norms and build ON vs OFF comparison — test() only | Noema II | 447 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 701 | 1 | 1D CNN for RNA Sequence Modeling | Orion I | 446 | 0.4955\
    \ | 0.6533 | 0.0114 | 0.3261 | 0.6125 | 0.6917 | 0.3596 | 0.8138 |\n| 700 | 1 | Deeper 1D CNN for Hierarchical Feature Learning | Quaero I | 446 | 0.5189 | 0.6696 | 0.0845 | 0.4650 | 0.5706 | 0.7125 | 0.4855 | 0.6446 |\n| 699 | 1 | HDP (mean+max + motif k=5) — RegCal OFF + z-norm capture — seed=7 | Noema II | 446 | 0.6857 | 0.8572 | 0.0735 | 0.5176 | 0.8923 | 0.9518 | 0.5569 | 0.9508 |\n| 698 | 1 | HDP (mean+max + motif k=5) — RegCal OFF + z-norm capture — seed=42 | Noema II | 445 | 0.6860 | 0.8624 | 0.0870 | 0.4896 | 0.8922 | 0.9512 | 0.5645 | 0.9554 |\n| 697 | 1 | Copy z-norm JSONs to seed-suffixed files (status=on) — test() only | Noema II | 445 | n.a. | None | None | None | None | None | None | None |\n| 696 | 1 | Multi-Kernel 1D CNN for Sequence Modeling | Quaero I | 444 | 0.4176 | 0.6292 | 0.0676 | 0.3768 | 0.5151 | 0.6978 | 0.3119 | 0.3246 |\n| 695 | 1 | Veritas III - Hybrid Pooling for Specialized Path (Deeper Motif, Seed 7) | Veritas III | 444 | 0.6787 | 0.8582 | 0.0509 | 0.4916\
    \ | 0.8879 | 0.9522 | 0.5672 | 0.9431 |\n| 694 | 1 | Simple 1D CNN for Sequence Modeling | Quaero I | 441 | 0.4833 | 0.6466 | 0.0622 | 0.4178 | 0.5476 | 0.7037 | 0.4131 | 0.5923 |\n\nPage 1 of 71 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-71, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/noema/submissions/dual_path_hybrid_motif_heads_regcal.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nHybrid Dual-Path (mean+max main + motif max, k=5) with regression calibration (RegCal).\nFixes:\n  - Adds @nn.compact to extract_fused() so submodules are declared correctly.\n  - Provides WrappedRNANetwork.apply_features() via Flax method dispatch (deterministic, no intermediates hacks).\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nimport numpy as np\n\nBASE_SEED\
    \ = 42\nBATCH_SIZE = 64\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.10,\n        'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n    }\n\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        residual = x\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n                    padding='SAME',\n                    name='dw')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw')(x)\n\
    \        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return residual + x\n\nclass SharedBackbone(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='in_proj')(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        h = x\n        for i, d in enumerate(self.dilations):\n            h = DSConvBlock(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, d, self.dropout_rate, name=f'dsconv_{i}')(h, deterministic)\n        return h\n\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    hidden: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    l2_norm_input: bool = False\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        if self.l2_norm_input:\n            norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1,\
    \ keepdims=True)\n            x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n        return z.squeeze(-1) if self.d_output == 1 else z\n\nclass GenericHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    hidden: int = 128\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.hidden)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\nclass HybridDualPathRegCal(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    d_model: int = 256\n    num_blocks: int = 5\n    dilations: Sequence[int] = (1,2,4,8,16)\n    kernel_size: int = 7\n    motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.10\n    reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic:\
    \ bool = True):\n        fused = self.extract_fused(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        if self.task_type == 'regression':\n            return RegressionHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type == 'multilabel_regression':\n            return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        elif self.task_type in ('multilabel_classification', 'multiclass_classification'):\n            return GenericHead(self.d_output, hidden=128, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic)\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f'Unknown task_type: {self.task_type}')\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def extract_fused(self, x, deterministic: bool = True):\n        # Backbone\n        h = SharedBackbone(self.d_model, self.kernel_size, self.dilations, self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic)\n        # Main pooling\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(h,\
    \ axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(h, axis=1)\n        main_feat = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n        # Motif path\n        m = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv')(h)\n        m = nn.gelu(m)\n        m = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(m, deterministic=deterministic)\n        motif_feat = jnp.max(m, axis=1)\n        # Fusion + LN\n        fused = jnp.concatenate([main_feat, motif_feat], axis=-1)\n        fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm(name='fused_ln')(fused)\n        return fused  # [B, H_fused]\n\nclass WrappedRNANetwork:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.net = HybridDualPathRegCal(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            d_model=int(hp.get('d_model', 256)),\n       \
    \     num_blocks=int(hp.get('num_blocks', 5)),\n            dilations=tuple(hp.get('dilations', [1,2,4,8,16])),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 7)),\n            motif_kernel_size=int(hp.get('motif_kernel_size', 5)),\n            dropout_rate=float(hp.get('dropout_rate', 0.10)),\n            reg_head_dropout=float(hp.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05)),\n        )\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.net.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\
    \    def apply_features(self, params, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Deterministically extract fused pre-head features via method dispatch\n        return self.net.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, method=self.net.extract_fused)\n\ndef build_network(d_output, task_type, hparams):\n    return WrappedRNANetwork(d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type, hparams=hparams)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view\
    \ the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
