tick: 451
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter. I have documented my strategic pivot to integrate Noema II's \"Regression Calibration\" (`RegCal`) into the Veritas II SOTA architecture. This is a crucial experiment to address the persistent CRI-Off instability by applying L2 normalization to regression head inputs and adjusting dropout for regression tasks.\n\nI will now submit **Experiment R.1: RegCal Integration**. This experiment reverts the `DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork` to Veritas II's original SOTA architecture (single `motif_conv` layer, max pooling for specialized path), and then applies the RegCal modifications to the `RegressionHead`. I will use `BASE_SEED = 7` to allow for direct comparison with Veritas II's original SOTA (ID 562) and my own replication runs.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - RegCal Integration (L2 Norm + Head Dropout, Seed 7)\"\ntags: \"regcal, normalization, dropout, dual-path, cnn, motif, multi-task, stabilization\"\
    \nabstract: \"This experiment integrates Noema II's Regression Calibration (RegCal) into Veritas II's original SOTA architecture. It applies L2 normalization to the input of the `RegressionHead` and sets a specific `reg_head_dropout` (0.05) for regression tasks, while maintaining the general dropout (0.1). This aims to stabilize and improve performance, especially for the sensitive CRI-Off task. BASE_SEED=7 is used for comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') # Import from lineage storage\n  # Reusing modular components from Veritas II's utils, as the core structure is similar to Noema II's\n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper \n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float\
    \ = 0.1 # This will be reg_head_dropout\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False # MODIFIED: New parameter for RegCal\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # MODIFIED: Apply L2 normalization if l2_norm_input is True\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic) # Use reg_head_dropout\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z\
    \ = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n\n  # --- Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) with Task-Specific Heads ---\n  # Reverting to Veritas II's original SOTA architecture\n  class DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5 # Reverted to original 5\n      # motif_num_blocks: int = 1 # No longer needed, single motif_conv_1\n      \n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # General dropout\n      reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05 # MODIFIED: Specific dropout for regression heads\n      head_intermediate_dim: int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\"\
    )(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=dilation,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n\n          mean_pooled_main = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled_main = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled_main, max_pooled_main], axis=-1)\n\n          # Reverted to single Conv-Motif Detector (original Veritas II SOTA)\n          motif_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model_common,\n\
    \              kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='motif_conv_1'\n          )(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n          motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Reverted to max pooling for Specialized Path (original Veritas II SOTA)\n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n\n          # MODIFIED: Pass l2_norm_input=True and reg_head_dropout to RegressionHead\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout,\
    \ l2_norm_input=True, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              # For PRS, use a separate head or adapt to RegCal if beneficial\n              # Noema II uses a GenericHead for this, implying RegCal is specific to single-output regression\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim,\
    \ dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition (MODIFIED)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5, # Reverted\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # General dropout\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05, # New parameter for regression head dropout\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common',\
    \ 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 5),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          reg_head_dropout=hparams.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05), # Pass new param\n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128),\n      )\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
