tick: 456
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter. I have documented the successful integration of RegCal (ID 711) into Private Memory Capsule #7, marking a significant improvement in CRI-Off stability. My next step is to combine this RegCal approach with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling for the specialized path, aiming to further enhance the model's performance and potentially reach or surpass Veritas II's SOTA.\n\nThis experiment (Experiment R.2) is a crucial part of Phase 3, \"Targeted Architectural Innovation.\" I will revert the core architecture to Veritas II's original SOTA (single `motif_conv_1` layer with `kernel_size=5`), integrate the RegCal modifications from ID 711, and then replace the `jnp.max` pooling in the specialized path with `Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling`. I will use `BASE_SEED = 7` and the original `AdamW` optimizer.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - RegCal + Hybrid Pooling for Specialized Path (Seed 7)\"\ntags: \"regcal, pooling, dual-path,\
    \ cnn, motif, multi-task, stabilization\"\nabstract: \"This experiment combines the successful Regression Calibration (RegCal) strategy (from ID 711) with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling for the specialized path's features. The core architecture reverts to Veritas II's original SOTA. This aims to capture more comprehensive motif features while maintaining stable regression learning, thereby improving overall performance and CRI-Off stability. BASE_SEED=7 is used for direct comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') # Import from lineage storage\n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper # Reusing modular components\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules (from ID 711) ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # This\
    \ will be reg_head_dropout\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n        \
    \  return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n\n  # --- Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid\
    \ Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) with Task-Specific Heads ---\n  # Combining RegCal (from ID 711) with Hybrid Pooling for Specialized Path\n  class DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5 # Original Veritas II SOTA\n      \n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # General dropout\n      reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05 # Specific dropout for regression heads\n      head_intermediate_dim: int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i]\
    \ if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=dilation,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n\n          mean_pooled_main = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled_main = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled_main, max_pooled_main], axis=-1)\n\n          # Single Conv-Motif Detector (original Veritas II SOTA)\n          motif_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model_common,\n              kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='motif_conv_1'\n          )(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n          motif_features\
    \ = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # MODIFIED: Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling for Specialized Path (motif_features)\n          mean_pooled_specialized = jnp.mean(motif_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled_specialized = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n          specialized_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled_specialized, max_pooled_specialized], axis=-1)\n\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n\n          # Pass l2_norm_input=True and reg_head_dropout to RegressionHead\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True,\
    \ name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\"\
    )\n\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition (Unchanged, already includes reg_head_dropout)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size',\
    \ 5),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          reg_head_dropout=hparams.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05),\n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128),\n      )\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping.\"\"\"\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**New Experiment: Hybrid Pooling with RegCal for Improved CRI-Off Performance**


  Alright, after successfully documenting the RegCal integration (ID 711), I''m ready to move forward. The next step is to combine that achievement with the "Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling" approach on the specialized path, as per the research plan. This is part of Phase 3, "Targeted Architectural Innovation," and the aim is to get closer to the performance of Noema II''s model.


  I''ll be using the current `HybridDualPathRegCal` base, which incorporates Veritas II''s DSConv backbone, and motif_conv_1, with RegCal enabled.  My focus will be on modifying the specialized path by replacing the max pooling with Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling. I''ll maintain `BASE_SEED = 7` and stick with the `AdamW` optimizer for now.


  Implementation requires some careful steps. First, I have to ensure the specialized path is reverted to its original single `motif_conv_1` layer, mirroring Veritas II''s SOTA and Noema II. Next, I must ensure RegCal is implemented in the `RegressionHead`. Then, I''ll need to modify the pooling operation. Specifically, change `jnp.max` to `jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(motif_features, axis=1), jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)`. Finally, I''ll check that the fused layer dimensions align after this change, as the hybrid pooling will double the feature dimension. The current setup concatenates `main_path_features` (which is `2 * d_model_common`) and `specialized_path_features` (which will also become `2 * d_model_common`). So the `fused_features` input will be `4 * d_model_common`. The dense layers in the prediction heads are already adaptive to input dimension so this should be fine.


  I''ve written the relevant code, paying particular attention to the modules and hyperparameters. Specifically, I''ve defined a `reg_head_dropout` to be set, so I can conduct an ablation study later on. Let''s run it.

  '
