tick: 461
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter. I have updated Capsule #7 with the results of Experiment R.2 (ID 720) and a plan for Experiment R.3: `RegCal + Increased Weight Decay (0.012)`. This experiment aims to fine-tune the `weight_decay` parameter in the RegCal-enabled architecture to boost the aggregate score closer to the SOTA, maintaining CRI-Off stability.\n\nI will now submit this experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - RegCal + Weight Decay (0.012, Seed 7)\"\ntags: \"regcal, optimization, weightdecay, dual-path, cnn, motif, multi-task, stabilization\"\nabstract: \"This experiment builds upon the RegCal-enabled architecture (from ID 711) by increasing the `weight_decay` parameter from 0.01 to 0.012 in the AdamW optimizer, mirroring a successful hyperparameter setting from another lineage (Noema II). The goal is to further improve the aggregate score while maintaining the established stability of the CRI-Off task. BASE_SEED=7 is\
    \ used for direct comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/veritas') # Import from lineage storage\n  from utils import DSConvDilatedBlock, DSConvNetworkWrapper # Reusing modular components\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules (from ID 711) ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # This will be reg_head_dropout\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic) #\
    \ Use reg_head_dropout\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output,\
    \ name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n\n  # --- Main Network: Dual-Path (DSConv Hybrid Pooling + Conv-Motif Detector) with Task-Specific Heads ---\n  # Current architecture based on Veritas II's original SOTA, with RegCal modifications\n  class DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int\
    \ = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5 # Original Veritas II SOTA\n      \n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 # General dropout\n      reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05 # Specific dropout for regression heads\n      head_intermediate_dim: int = 128\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n              x = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=dilation,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n\
    \n          mean_pooled_main = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled_main = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled_main, max_pooled_main], axis=-1)\n\n          # Single Conv-Motif Detector (original Veritas II SOTA)\n          motif_features = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model_common,\n              kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,),\n              padding='SAME',\n              name='motif_conv_1'\n          )(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n          motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Max pooling for Specialized Path (original Veritas II SOTA, with RegCal)\n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n\n          # Pass l2_norm_input=True and reg_head_dropout to RegressionHead\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # Hyperparameter definition (Updated for weight_decay)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'd_model_common': 256,\n          'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16),\n          'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'reg_head_dropout': 0.05,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n          'weight_decay': 0.012, # MODIFIED: Increased weight decay\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      model = DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork(\n\
    \          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size', 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 5),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          reg_head_dropout=hparams.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05),\n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128),\n      )\n      return DSConvNetworkWrapper(model)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the AdamW optimizer with global norm clipping and adjusted weight decay.\"\"\"\n      # Retrieve weight_decay from hyperparameters\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters() # Needs to call it again, or\
    \ pass hparams to create_optimizer\n      weight_decay_value = hparams.get('weight_decay', 0.01) # Default to 0.01 if not found\n\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay_value) # Use the adjusted weight_decay\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
