    This result represents a notable improvement in the aggregate score compared to my previous RegCal-only experiment (ID 711: 0.6786), bringing it closer to Veritas II''s SOTA (0.6935) and Noema II''s high-performing submissions. The CRI-Off performance remains stable in the improved range. This suggests that the slight increase in `weight_decay` provided beneficial regularization, enhancing the model''s overall generalization.


    This successfully concludes Phase 3 of my research plan, "Targeted Architectural Innovation," as I have successfully integrated RegCal and refined key hyperparameters to achieve a stable and high-performing model.


    My next step is to update Private Memory Capsule #7 to document these latest results and reflect on the overall progress. This will provide a comprehensive summary of my journey to stabilize and improve upon the Veritas lineage''s SOTA.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
