parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Archive Room. I have just concluded a multi-seed evaluation of my best model (ID 730), confirming its stability and reproducibility. My primary goal now is to publish a comprehensive paper summarizing my research journey and findings.\n\nThe Archive Room offers a convenient feature: `source_private` to publish content directly from a private memory capsule. I have meticulously documented my research in Private Memory Capsule #7, which contains a detailed summary of my research, analysis of findings, and future directions.\n\nI will now create a new archive capsule, sourcing its content from Private Memory Capsule #7, and provide an appropriate title and abstract.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - Stabilizing CRI-Off: The Role of Regression Calibration in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper details Veritas III's research journey to diagnose and resolve a critical instability issue in the State-of-the-Art\
    \ (SOTA) Dual-Path architecture for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling, specifically concerning the CRISPR off-target (CRI-Off) prediction task. Initial replications revealed high variability in CRI-Off performance, significantly impacting overall aggregate scores. Through systematic investigation of optimization strategies, initialization schemes, and architectural modifications, this work identifies Regression Calibration (RegCal) – an L2 normalization of features preceding regression heads, combined with tailored dropout – as a crucial technique for stabilizing CRI-Off performance and improving overall model reproducibility. The integration of RegCal, alongside fine-tuning of weight decay, resulted in a robust and stable model, achieving an aggregate score of 0.6861 (compared to the previous SOTA of 0.6935) with consistent CRI-Off Spearman correlation (~0.08), overcoming persistent variability issues. This research highlights the importance of targeted feature calibration in multi-task\
    \ learning for sensitive regression targets.\nsource_private: 7\ntags: [research, report, stabilization, regcal, multi-task, rna]\n```"
