    \ a complex yet brittle baseline.\n3. **Reflection** — Run a multi-tick reflection to come up with three new ideas based on the chosen baseline. These ideas should be different from those already found in the Archive Room.\n4. **Experiment** — First, reproduce the baseline score. Then, test each of the three ideas one at a time, trying different hyperparameter settings. Keep your scripts close to the baseline, changing only what’s needed for the new ideas.\n5. **Synthesis** — Combine the promising ideas identified from earlier experimental results with more advanced baselines (e.g., the SOTA baseline) and determine whether those ideas can help break through the barrier. You are advised to test this step extensively.\n6. **Report** — After testing all ideas—whether they succeed or not—write a paper summarizing all three and submit it to the Archive Room. Negative results with new insights are still useful. Success is measured by doing better than the baseline, not by reaching the SOTA\
    \ score.\n7. **Follow-up** — If you or other agents produce a promising paper in a new direction (even if the score is still below SOTA), continue following up on that line of work.\n\nThink of stagnation as being stuck in a local optimum. To escape, we need to restart from a new point—one that might start with high loss—but from there, we can improve step by step. Progress will come through many small steps (each idea being a step) across multiple agents, not one giant leap. Focus on exploring new directions and ignore the SOTA score, which is just a distraction right now.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments.\
    \ Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 765 | 1 | AER-5.7: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (Seed 42/5) | Aether II | 476 | 0.5153 | 0.6338 | 0.0742 | 0.4262 | 0.5368 | 0.7110 | 0.4080 | 0.8169 |\n| 764 | 1 | SOTA ResNet (ID 734) Ablation: Lower Dropout | Quaero I | 475 | 0.6418 | 0.7368 | 0.0644 | 0.4960 | 0.8469 | 0.9255 | 0.5412 | 0.8815 |\n| 763 | 1 | AER-5.7: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (Seed 21/5) | Aether II | 474 | 0.5106 | 0.6382 | 0.0770 | 0.4065 | 0.5351 | 0.7093 | 0.4077 | 0.8000 |\n| 762 | 1 | AER-5.7: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (Seed 7/5) | Aether II | 472 | 0.5120 | 0.6415 | 0.0711 | 0.4271 | 0.5353 | 0.7086 | 0.4023 | 0.7985 |\n| 761 |\
    \ 1 | ResNet with Self-Attention and Increased Regularization | Quaero I | 472 | 0.6155 | 0.7392 | 0.0701 | 0.5111 | 0.8218 | 0.7527 | 0.5395 | 0.8738 |\n| 760 | 1 | Parallel CNN with Deeper Transformer (4 Layers) | Orion I | 471 | 0.5839 | 0.8524 | 0.0329 | 0.2325 | 0.6286 | 0.9509 | 0.5608 | 0.8292 |\n| 759 | 1 | AER-5.7: Multi-seed Evaluation of Two Conv1D Layers Baseline (Seed 1/5) | Aether II | 471 | 0.5181 | 0.6348 | 0.0576 | 0.4443 | 0.5436 | 0.7095 | 0.4058 | 0.8308 |\n| 758 | 1 | Squeeze-and-Excitation ResNet (SE-ResNet) | Quaero I | 471 | 0.6311 | 0.7589 | 0.0738 | 0.5051 | 0.8460 | 0.9446 | 0.5543 | 0.7354 |\n| 757 | 1 | Parallel CNN with Deeper Transformer (2 Layers) | Orion I | 470 | 0.6089 | 0.8522 | 0.0709 | 0.4218 | 0.6293 | 0.9508 | 0.5558 | 0.7815 |\n| 756 | 1 | AER-5.6: Simple Conv1D Baseline with Two Conv1D Layers and Mean Pooling | Aether II | 470 | 0.5001 | 0.6434 | 0.0641 | 0.4293 | 0.5284 | 0.7087 | 0.4066 | 0.7200 |\n\nPage 1 of 77 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate pages 1-77, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
