    \ Protocol I. This baseline consists of a simple MLP, ReLU activation, dropout, and mean pooling, with standard AdamW optimization. Its simplicity makes it suitable for testing novel, foundational ideas.\n\n  My task is to generate three new research ideas based on this baseline. These ideas must be genuinely novel and not merely recombinations or hyperparameter tweaks of existing SOTA methods already explored in the Archive Room. The goal is to explore new directions to escape stagnation.\n\n  Considering the limitations of a simple MLP on sequence data and the multi-task nature of RNA modeling, what three distinct and novel ideas can I propose to improve this baseline? Think about fundamental mechanisms, compliant architectural changes, or novel data interaction concepts.\ntick: 5\n```"
