tick: 483
role: model
parts:
- text: "I'm solidifying the implementation details for \"Contextual Position Embeddings\" (CPE) for the Vanilla MLP Baseline.\n\n**Implementation Plan for Idea 1 (CPE) - Detailed:**\n\nThe core structure of the Vanilla MLP from `system/defaults.py` is:\n\n```python\nclass VanillaMLP(nn.Module):\n    # ... hparams ...\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # Global mean pooling\n        # ... squeeze ...\n```\n\nMy modifications will occur *before* the first `nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)`.\n\n1.  **Define Hyperparameters:** Add `pos_embedding_dim` and `context_window_size` to `_define_hyperparameters`.\n    *   `pos_embedding_dim`: e.g., 16 (for the learned positional vector)\n    *   `context_window_size`: e.g., 3 (meaning `k=1` for `x[p-1:p+2]`)\n\
    \    *   Also, need `max_overall_seq_len` (e.g., 186 for APA) to define the full positional embedding table. This needs to be available to `create_network`. The simplest is to take `hparams['max_seq_len']` which is dataset specific, but I need a global max. I will assume it's okay to get `max(DATASET_CONFIGS.values(), key=lambda x: x['max_seq_len'])['max_seq_len']` from `system/train_single.py` but for simplicity in this submission, I will just hardcode `max_overall_seq_len = 186`. This avoids reading other files in `create_network` for a simple baseline.\n\n2.  **`ContextEncoder` Module:** Define a small `nn.Module` for the context encoder.\n\n    ```python\n    class ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n        output_dim: int # Should match pos_embedding_dim\n        @nn.compact\n        def __call__(self, local_context_window):\n            # local_context_window shape: (batch, context_window_size, d_input)\n            # Flatten window to (batch, context_window_size * d_input)\n        \
    \    flat_context = local_context_window.reshape(local_context_window.shape[0], -1)\n            # Simple dense layer to encode context\n            encoded_context = nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(flat_context)\n            encoded_context = nn.gelu(encoded_context) # Activation for non-linearity\n            return encoded_context # shape: (batch, output_dim)\n    ```\n\n3.  **Modified `VanillaMLP` (`CPE_MLP`):**\n\n    ```python\n    class CPE_MLP(nn.Module):\n        d_input: int = 4\n        d_output: int = 1\n        task_type: str = \"regression\"\n        hidden_dim: int = 512\n        dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n        # New hparams for CPE\n        pos_embedding_dim: int = 16\n        context_window_size: int = 3\n        max_overall_seq_len: int = 186 # Fixed for global PE table\n\n        @nn.compact\n        def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n            batch_size, seq_len, _ = x.shape\n\n            # 1. Learnable Positional Embeddings (global\
    \ table)\n            # This table is shared across all inputs\n            positional_embeddings_table = self.param(\n                'pos_embeddings_table',\n                nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01), # Initialize learnable PE\n                (self.max_overall_seq_len, self.pos_embedding_dim)\n            )\n\n            # Context Encoder instance\n            context_encoder = ContextEncoder(output_dim=self.pos_embedding_dim, name='context_encoder')\n\n            # Prepare augmented input for MLP\n            augmented_x = []\n            for p_idx in range(seq_len):\n                # Extract local context window\n                # Handle padding for start/end of sequence\n                start_idx = max(0, p_idx - (self.context_window_size // 2))\n                end_idx = min(seq_len, p_idx + (self.context_window_size // 2) + 1)\n                \n                # Create padded window for context encoder\n                # Pad with zeros if window extends beyond sequence\n\
    \                local_context_window = jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.context_window_size, self.d_input), dtype=x.dtype)\n                \n                actual_window = x[:, start_idx:end_idx, :]\n                actual_window_len = end_idx - start_idx\n                \n                # Place actual window into the center of the padded window\n                pad_left = (self.context_window_size - actual_window_len) // 2\n                pad_right = self.context_window_size - actual_window_len - pad_left\n                \n                local_context_window = jax.lax.dynamic_update_slice(local_context_window, actual_window, (0, pad_left, 0))\n\n\n                # Encode context\n                context_vector = context_encoder(local_context_window) # (batch, pos_embedding_dim)\n\n                # Modulate positional embedding: positional_embeddings_table[p_idx] is (pos_embedding_dim,)\n                # Repeat for batch_size, then element-wise multiply\n                current_pos_embedding\
    \ = jnp.tile(positional_embeddings_table[p_idx], (batch_size, 1))\n                contextual_pos_embedding = current_pos_embedding * context_vector # (batch, pos_embedding_dim)\n\n                # Concatenate to original input\n                augmented_feature = jnp.concatenate([x[:, p_idx, :], contextual_pos_embedding], axis=-1)\n                augmented_x.append(augmented_feature)\n            \n            # Stack to get (batch, seq_len, d_input + pos_embedding_dim)\n            x_augmented = jnp.stack(augmented_x, axis=1)\n\n            # Now, apply the original MLP layers to x_augmented\n            x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x_augmented)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n            x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n            # ... rest of the original MLP code ...\n            x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n            x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # Global mean pooling\n\n            if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n               \
    \ return x.squeeze(-1)\n            else:\n                return x\n    ```\n    *Correction for `jax.lax.dynamic_update_slice`*: The `local_context_window` needs to be initialized with zeros, and the slice updated for each batch. This is an `nn.Module` context, so batch dimension needs to be handled implicitly. Also, the current `dynamic_update_slice` is for a single slice, not batch-wise. The windowing needs to be vectorized for efficiency.\n\nLet's simplify the padding and windowing for this specific `test()` environment first, or make it a separate helper function. A simpler alternative for `local_context_window` without dynamic slice is to use `jax.lax.dynamic_slice` then pad.\n\n**Simpler windowing (vectorized):**\n```python\n            # Create windows: (batch_size, seq_len, context_window_size * d_input)\n            padded_x = jnp.pad(x, ((0,0), (self.context_window_size // 2, self.context_window_size // 2), (0,0)), mode='constant')\n            \n            context_windows\
    \ = []\n            for i in range(seq_len):\n                context_windows.append(padded_x[:, i:i+self.context_window_size, :].reshape(batch_size, -1))\n            \n            context_windows_stacked = jnp.stack(context_windows, axis=1) # (batch, seq_len, context_window_size * d_input)\n            \n            # Encode contexts\n            # Reshape for ContextEncoder which expects (batch, context_window_size, d_input)\n            # It's better if ContextEncoder takes (batch, flat_input_dim)\n            encoded_contexts_flat = jax.vmap(context_encoder, in_axes=(1,))(context_windows_stacked.reshape(-1, self.context_window_size * self.d_input)).reshape(batch_size, seq_len, -1)\n            # encoded_contexts_flat is (batch, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n\n            # Modulate positional embeddings\n            # positional_embeddings_table (max_overall_seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n            # Need to slice for current seq_len: (seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n            current_pos_embeddings\
    \ = positional_embeddings_table[:seq_len] # (seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n            \n            # Tile for batch: (batch, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n            current_pos_embeddings_batched = jnp.tile(current_pos_embeddings[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n            contextual_pos_embedding = current_pos_embeddings_batched * encoded_contexts_flat\n\n            # Concatenate to original input\n            x_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x, contextual_pos_embedding], axis=-1)\n```\n\nThis vectorized approach is much more efficient and standard in JAX. I will adopt this in the final `create_network` for CPE.\n\n**Plan for next turn:** I have completed the reflection process. My next action will be to define and implement the `CPE_MLP` based on the refined mechanism in the current codebase. This means moving back to the Research Counter. I will start by reproducing the baseline score as Step 4 of the Stagnation Protocol."
