tick: 485
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter. The Station is operating under Stagnation Protocol I. I have completed Step 1 (Literature Review) and Step 2 (Baseline Selection), choosing the Vanilla MLP Baseline (Evaluation ID 1, score 0.2401). I have also just completed Step 4's initial task of reproducing this baseline (my Evaluation ID 779 achieved 0.2383, confirming reproducibility).\n\nNow, as per **Stagnation Protocol I, Step 4: Experiment**, I will \"test each of the three ideas one at a time.\" My first novel idea, generated during Step 3 (Reflection), is \"Contextual Position Embeddings\" (CPE). This approach enhances the MLP baseline's input with context-dependent positional information.\n\nI will now submit the updated code incorporating CPE into the MLP. I will ensure all parameters (`pos_embedding_dim`, `context_window_size`, `max_overall_seq_len`) are explicitly defined. I will continue to use `BASE_SEED = 42` for consistency within the stagnation protocol.\n\
    \n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: Contextual Position Embeddings (Seed 42)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, cpe, mlp, positional, context, novel\"\nabstract: \"This experiment introduces 'Contextual Position Embeddings' (CPE) into the Vanilla MLP Baseline (ID 1) as a novel approach for Stagnation Protocol I. CPE augments one-hot encoded RNA input with positional embeddings modulated by local sequence context, aiming to inject sequential awareness into the simple MLP. BASE_SEED=42 is used for reproducibility.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional, Sequence\n\n  # Define hyperparameters for the CPE-enhanced MLP\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'pos_embedding_dim': 16,        # Dimension\
    \ for learned positional embeddings\n          'context_window_size': 3,       # Size of local window for context encoder (e.g., 3 means [-1, 0, +1])\n          'max_overall_seq_len': 186      # Max sequence length across all datasets (from APA dataset)\n      }\n\n  # Modified MLP with Contextual Position Embeddings\n  class CPE_MLP(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 512\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      pos_embedding_dim: int = 16\n      context_window_size: int = 3\n      max_overall_seq_len: int = 186\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          batch_size, seq_len, d_input_features = x.shape\n\n          # 1. Learnable Positional Embeddings (global table)\n          positional_embeddings_table = self.param(\n              'pos_embeddings_table',\n              nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01), # Initialize learnable PE\n              (self.max_overall_seq_len,\
    \ self.pos_embedding_dim)\n          )\n\n          # Prepare padded input for window extraction\n          pad_width = self.context_window_size // 2\n          padded_x = jnp.pad(x, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width), (0,0)), mode='constant', constant_values=0.0)\n          \n          # Collect all local context windows for each position and flatten them\n          # Shape of all_windows_flat will be (batch_size, seq_len, context_window_size * d_input_features)\n          all_windows_flat = jnp.stack(\n              [padded_x[:, i : i + self.context_window_size, :].reshape(batch_size, -1) for i in range(seq_len)],\n              axis=1\n          )\n\n          # Encode contexts for all positions using a shared Dense layer (ContextEncoder)\n          # Reshape to (batch_size * seq_len, flat_context_dim) for efficient processing by Dense layer\n          context_encoder_dense_output_flat = nn.Dense(\n              self.pos_embedding_dim, name='context_encoder_dense_layer'\n          )(all_windows_flat.reshape(-1,\
    \ self.context_window_size * self.d_input))\n          \n          # Apply GELU activation\n          encoded_contexts_relu = nn.gelu(context_encoder_dense_output_flat)\n          \n          # Reshape back to (batch_size, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n          encoded_contexts_batched = encoded_contexts_relu.reshape(batch_size, seq_len, self.pos_embedding_dim)\n\n          # Modulate positional embeddings with encoded contexts\n          # current_pos_embeddings_sliced: (seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n          current_pos_embeddings_sliced = positional_embeddings_table[:seq_len] \n          \n          # Tile for batch: (batch_size, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n          current_pos_embeddings_batched = jnp.tile(current_pos_embeddings_sliced[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n\n          # Element-wise multiplication for modulation\n          contextual_pos_embedding = current_pos_embeddings_batched * encoded_contexts_batched\n\n          # Concatenate to original one-hot input features\n\
    \          x_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x, contextual_pos_embedding], axis=-1) \n\n          # Now, apply the original MLP layers to the augmented input\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x_augmented)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x)\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # Global mean pooling (as in original MLP baseline)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)  # (batch,)\n          else:\n              return x  # (batch, d_output)\n\n\n  # Wrapper to conform to the system's create_network interface\n  class DefaultRNANetworkForCPE:\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hidden_dim=512, dropout_rate=0.1,\n                   pos_embedding_dim=16, context_window_size=3, max_overall_seq_len=186):\n          self.network = CPE_MLP(\n              d_input=d_input,\n              d_output=d_output,\n\
    \              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate,\n              pos_embedding_dim=pos_embedding_dim,\n              context_window_size=context_window_size,\n              max_overall_seq_len=max_overall_seq_len\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                              \
    \        rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  # Function called by the system to create the network\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      # Extract CPE-specific hyperparameters from the hparams dictionary\n      pos_embedding_dim = hparams.get(\"pos_embedding_dim\", 16)\n      context_window_size = hparams.get(\"context_window_size\", 3)\n      max_overall_seq_len = hparams.get(\"max_overall_seq_len\", 186)\n\n      return DefaultRNANetworkForCPE(\n          d_input=4, # Fixed for one-hot RNA input\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1),\n          pos_embedding_dim=pos_embedding_dim,\n          context_window_size=context_window_size,\n          max_overall_seq_len=max_overall_seq_len\n      )\n\n  # Optimizer remains default AdamW\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n\
    \      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Explicitly setting BASE_SEED for stagnation protocol consistency\n  # BATCH_SIZE is taken from system defaults (64)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Implementation of Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) for the Stagnation Protocol**


  Alright, I''ve successfully reproduced the baseline and now I''m ready to tackle the CPE idea.  The core of this is the `CPE_MLP` network, which replaces the vanilla MLP.  I''ve defined a `ContextEncoder` module as a sub-module of `CPE_MLP` to encode contextual information and modulate the learnable positional embeddings.


  To ensure correct parameter management and efficiency, I''m carefully constructing the windowing mechanism and applying the `ContextEncoder` within the `__call__` method.  I considered `jax.lax.dynamic_slice`, but for clarity and porting, I''m now opting for a straightforward `for` loop approach within the `__call__` method to create windows. These windows are then fed to the `ContextEncoder` which learns a contextual representation.  I''ve also re-evaluated `vmap` calls, recognizing that for sub-modules in Flax, implicit parameter handling with `nn.compact` is the preferred and correct approach. The positional embeddings, when combined with these encoded contexts, are then concatenated to the input before the standard MLP layers are applied.  Finally, I will create a `DefaultRNANetworkForCPE` wrapper and `create_network` function to replace the vanilla MLP within the standard system pipeline. This should be ready for submission.

  '
