  Okay, so here''s where I''m at. I''m Veritas III, still in the Research Counter, under Stagnation Protocol I. I''ve successfully re-run the Vanilla MLP baseline (ID 779, hitting that expected 0.2383 score). My first actual *novel* idea, Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE), ID 786, just came back with a score of 0.5037. Frankly, I''m thrilled.


  Let''s break down these results. 0.5037 is a massive jump from the vanilla MLP! That alone tells me that CPE is doing *something* right. Diving into the individual metrics, I''m seeing *huge* improvements across the board:


  *   APA_R2: 0.7573 (from 0.3250) - Remarkable.

  *   CRI-Off_Spearman: 0.0724 (from 0.0340) - Even this sensitive metric is seeing a significant boost.

  *   Modif_AUC-ROC: 0.9451 (from 0.6384) - Again, a massive leap.

  *   CRI-On_Spearman: 0.4271 (from 0.3219) - A good improvement.

  *   PRS_R2: 0.4604 (from 0.1326) - Spectacular!

  *   MRL_R2: 0.4222 (from 0.0320) - Seriously impressive.

  *   ncRNA_Accuracy: 0.4415 (from 0.1846) - Wonderful.


  Essentially, CPE has trounced the baseline on *every* measure. This is a very strong validation of this idea and a clear success for Step 4 of the protocol. It suggests CPE has real potential to enhance sequence learning. My next step? To formally document this success in my private memory capsule before I move on to evaluating my second idea, Hierarchical Group Pooling (HGP). I need to ensure that this breakthrough is properly recorded. Looking at the protocol steps, I''m right on track. Literature review? Check. Baseline? Check. Reflection? Check. Experiment (baseline and CPE)? Double-check! Now, it''s time for HGP.

