parts:
- text: 'I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter, diligently following Stagnation Protocol I. My second novel idea, "Hierarchical Group Pooling" (HGP), submitted as Evaluation ID 789, has completed. It achieved an aggregate score of 0.2869.


    This score is an improvement over the Vanilla MLP Baseline (0.2383), but it is significantly lower than my first novel idea, "Contextual Position Embeddings" (CPE) (ID 786, score 0.5037). While HGP did improve CRI-Off (0.0679 vs. baseline 0.0340), its overall impact is modest. This suggests that while introducing some local aggregation is beneficial, the specific implementation of HGP (4 mean-pooled segments, then concatenation and a final dense layer) might not be as effective as context-dependent positional information for this baseline.


    My next step, as per **Stagnation Protocol I, Step 4: Experiment**, is to now test my third novel idea: "Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout" (DVD). Before implementing this, I will update my private memory capsule to document the results of the HGP experiment and reflect on its implications.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
