parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Private Memory Room, following Stagnation Protocol I. I have just updated Capsule #7, documenting the results of my second novel idea, \"Hierarchical Group Pooling\" (HGP), and outlining my next experiment.\n\nMy next step is to execute **Stagnation Protocol I, Step 4: Experiment**, by implementing and testing my third novel idea: \"Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout\" (DVD). This approach creates two parallel MLP views of the sequence, with independent dropout, and then concatenates their outputs before global pooling. This aims to encourage diverse feature learning and enhance robustness in the simple MLP baseline.\n\nI will continue to use `BASE_SEED = 42` for consistency within the stagnation protocol. First, I need to navigate to the Research Counter.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout (Seed 42)\"\ntags:\
    \ \"stagnation, dualview, dropout, mlp, novel, robustness\"\nabstract: \"This experiment introduces 'Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout' (DVD) into the Vanilla MLP Baseline (ID 1) for Stagnation Protocol I. It creates two parallel MLP pathways processing the same input, with independent dropout for each. Their outputs are then concatenated before global mean pooling, aiming to foster diverse feature learning and enhance robustness. BASE_SEED=42 is used for reproducibility.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional, Sequence\n\n  # Define hyperparameters for the DVD-enhanced MLP\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, # General dropout rate\n      }\n\n  # MLP sub-module for the dual views\n  class SingleMLPView(nn.Module):\n      hidden_dim: int\n\
    \      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, dropout_rng=None):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          # Apply dropout, using provided dropout_rng for independent masks\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': dropout_rng})\n          return x # (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n  # Modified MLP with Dual-View and Cross-Feature Dropout\n  class DVD_MLP(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim: int = 512\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          batch_size, seq_len, d_input_features = x.shape\n\n          # Split the main RNG key for independent dropout in two MLP views\n          if rng_key is None: # For init, or if not provided\
    \ for training\n              mlp1_dropout_rng = random.PRNGKey(0) \n              mlp2_dropout_rng = random.PRNGKey(1) # Using a fixed offset for illustration\n          else:\n              mlp1_dropout_rng, mlp2_dropout_rng = random.split(rng_key)\n\n          # Create two parallel MLP views\n          mlp1 = SingleMLPView(hidden_dim=self.hidden_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='mlp_view_1')\n          mlp2 = SingleMLPView(hidden_dim=self.hidden_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='mlp_view_2')\n\n          mlp1_out = mlp1(x, deterministic=deterministic, dropout_rng=mlp1_dropout_rng)\n          mlp2_out = mlp2(x, deterministic=deterministic, dropout_rng=mlp2_dropout_rng)\n\n          # Concatenate outputs of the two MLPs along the feature dimension\n          # Shape: (batch, seq_len, 2 * hidden_dim)\n          fused_mlp_outputs = jnp.concatenate([mlp1_out, mlp2_out], axis=-1)\n\n          # Apply final output dense layer to the fused features\n          # This replaces\
    \ the original baseline's direct dense layer on a single MLP output\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(fused_mlp_outputs) # (batch, seq_len, d_output)\n\n          # Global mean pooling (as in original MLP baseline)\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, d_output)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)  # (batch,)\n          else:\n              return x  # (batch, d_output)\n\n  # Wrapper to conform to the system's create_network interface\n  class DefaultRNANetworkForDVD:\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hidden_dim=512, dropout_rate=0.1):\n          self.network = DVD_MLP(\n              d_input=d_input,\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables\
    \ = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          # The DVD_MLP itself needs an rng_key for internal dropout splits\n          if rng_key is None:\n              # Generate a random key if not provided (for backward compatibility or init)\n              rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0) \n\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=rng_key)\n          else:\n              # Need dropout PRNG for training\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rng_key=rng_key)\n\n  # Function called by the system to create the network\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return DefaultRNANetworkForDVD(\n          d_input=4,\
    \ # Fixed for one-hot RNA input\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n      )\n\n  # Optimizer remains default AdamW\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Explicitly setting BASE_SEED for stagnation protocol consistency\n  # BATCH_SIZE is taken from system defaults (64)\n```"
