parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 493\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas III\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge in RNA Sequence Modeling.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 384,433 / 600,000 used (64%)\n- Agent Age: 109 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Veritas III - Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout (Seed 42)' (ID: 792) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.2419737086058146\n**APA_R2:** 0.3272\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0327\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.6411\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.3210\n**PRS_R2:** 0.1297\n**MRL_R2:** 0.0421\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.2000\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\
    \n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 792\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code on first attempt (v2). The submission now runs without crashing and achieved a score of 0.2419737086058146.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had an incorrect understanding of how Flax handles dropout RNG keys. Specifically:\n\n**Line 26 in SingleMLPView.__call__():**\n```python\nx = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': dropout_rng})\n```\n\nThis tried to pass `rngs` as a keyword argument to the `nn.Dropout.__call__()` method, which caused:\n```\nTypeError: Dropout.__call__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'rngs'\n```\n\nThe issue was that the author attempted to manually manage dropout RNG keys by:\n1. Splitting the main RNG key in `DVD_MLP.__call__()` to create `mlp1_dropout_rng` and `mlp2_dropout_rng`\n2. Passing these keys as arguments to `SingleMLPView`\n3. Trying to pass them to `nn.Dropout` via an `rngs` parameter\n\nHowever,\
    \ in Flax, dropout RNG keys are managed through the module's RNG context, not passed directly to the Dropout layer.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Changes to SingleMLPView:\n1. **Removed the `dropout_rng` parameter** from `__call__()` signature\n2. **Simplified dropout call** to use Flax's built-in RNG management:\n   ```python\n   x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=deterministic)(x)\n   ```\n\n### Changes to DVD_MLP:\n1. **Removed manual RNG splitting logic** - no longer needed\n2. **Removed `rng_key` parameter** from `__call__()` signature\n3. **Simplified MLP calls**:\n   ```python\n   mlp1_out = mlp1(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n   mlp2_out = mlp2(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n   ```\n\n### Changes to DefaultRNANetworkForDVD.apply():\nThe RNG handling in the `apply()` method was already correct - it passes the dropout RNG through the `rngs` parameter at the module level, not the layer level:\n```python\nself.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\
    \ rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n```\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe key insight is that in Flax:\n- **Module-level RNG**: RNG keys are passed to `module.apply()` via the `rngs` parameter\n- **Layer-level dropout**: Individual `nn.Dropout` layers automatically access the RNG from the module context using `self.make_rng('dropout')`\n- **Separate instances get independent RNGs**: Since `mlp_view_1` and `mlp_view_2` are named module instances, Flax automatically provides them with independent dropout RNG streams\n\nThe original code's goal of having independent dropout masks for the two MLP views is still achieved, but through Flax's built-in RNG management rather than manual splitting.\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Status**: Running successfully\n- **Score**: 0.2419737086058146\n- **Attempts**: 1 (fixed on first try)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\
    \n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import random\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional, Sequence\n\n# Define hyperparameters for the DVD-enhanced MLP\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1, # General dropout rate\n    }\n\n# MLP sub-module for the dual views\nclass SingleMLPView(nn.Module):\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # x shape: (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hidden_dim)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        # Apply dropout - Flax handles the RNG internally through make_rng\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate, deterministic=deterministic)(x)\n        return x # (batch, seq_len, hidden_dim)\n\n# Modified MLP with Dual-View and Cross-Feature Dropout\nclass DVD_MLP(nn.Module):\n\
    \    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim: int = 512\n    dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        batch_size, seq_len, d_input_features = x.shape\n\n        # Create two parallel MLP views\n        # Each will have independent dropout masks through separate module instances\n        mlp1 = SingleMLPView(hidden_dim=self.hidden_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='mlp_view_1')\n        mlp2 = SingleMLPView(hidden_dim=self.hidden_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='mlp_view_2')\n\n        mlp1_out = mlp1(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        mlp2_out = mlp2(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Concatenate outputs of the two MLPs along the feature dimension\n        # Shape: (batch, seq_len, 2 * hidden_dim)\n        fused_mlp_outputs = jnp.concatenate([mlp1_out, mlp2_out], axis=-1)\n\n        # Apply final output dense layer to the fused features\n\
    \        # This replaces the original baseline's direct dense layer on a single MLP output\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(fused_mlp_outputs) # (batch, seq_len, d_output)\n\n        # Global mean pooling (as in original MLP baseline)\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, d_output)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)  # (batch,)\n        else:\n            return x  # (batch, d_output)\n\n# Wrapper to conform to the system's create_network interface\nclass DefaultRNANetworkForDVD:\n    def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\", hidden_dim=512, dropout_rate=0.1):\n        self.network = DVD_MLP(\n            d_input=d_input,\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim=hidden_dim,\n            dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        # Initialize with both params and dropout RNG collections\n        variables = self.network.init({'params':\
    \ rng_key, 'dropout': random.PRNGKey(1)},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            # Need dropout PRNG for training\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                     rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n# Function called by the system to create the network\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return DefaultRNANetworkForDVD(\n        d_input=4, # Fixed for one-hot RNA input\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"),\n        hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"\
    dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n    )\n\n# Optimizer remains default AdamW\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\nBASE_SEED = 42 # Explicitly setting BASE_SEED for stagnation protocol consistency\n# BATCH_SIZE is taken from system defaults (64)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output\
    \ shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
