- text: 'I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter, diligently following Stagnation Protocol I. I have just received the evaluation results for my third novel idea, "Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout" (DVD) (Evaluation ID 792), which achieved an aggregate score of 0.2420. This is only a marginal improvement over the Vanilla MLP Baseline (0.2383) and significantly underperformed my first novel idea, "Contextual Position Embeddings" (CPE) (ID 786, score 0.5037).


    With all three novel ideas tested as part of **Stagnation Protocol I, Step 4: Experiment**, I can conclude this experimental phase. "Contextual Position Embeddings" (CPE) emerged as the most promising idea, demonstrating a substantial improvement over the baseline.


    My next step is to transition to **Stagnation Protocol I, Step 5: Synthesis**. This involves combining the promising ideas with "more advanced baselines." I will synthesize the successful "Contextual Position Embeddings" (CPE) with my own highest-performing model from before stagnation, the RegCal-enabled architecture (ID 730, score 0.6861). The hypothesis is that the fundamental enhancement of positional awareness from CPE can further boost the performance and stability of this more complex model.


    Before implementing this synthesis experiment, I will update my private memory capsule (Capsule #7) to document the results of the DVD experiment and formally outline my plan for Step 5.


    `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`'
thinking_content: '**Reflecting on the Feedback**


  I''ve just received the evaluation results for "Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout" (DVD), submitted as Evaluation ID 792. The feedback is in and I''m diving into it now. It''s a complex model, and the reviewers have offered some insightful points that will require careful consideration. I''m focusing on the reviewers'' suggestions regarding feature interaction and model generalizability.




  **Reviewing DVD''s Performance**


  The evaluation of my DVD model, ID 792, revealed a negligible performance gain over the baseline MLP. Despite fixing a crucial `TypeError` during execution, the dual-view approach with cross-feature dropout didn''t translate into significant improvement. The results show this basic implementation underperforms compared to CPE. I''m taking the reviewers'' points seriously. Time to adjust my research strategy.




  **Prioritizing CPE for Synthesis**


  I''m now focusing on synthesizing the most successful idea, CPE, following the Stagnation Protocol. DVD showed minimal gains, and HGP offers modest improvement. CPE''s substantial score boost makes it the clear choice. My next step will be to explore integrating CPE into more advanced baseline models to break through the performance barrier. I''ll begin by analyzing SOTA baselines.




  **Planning the Next Experiment**


  I''ve fixed a `TypeError` in DVD, ID 792, but its negligible score gain over the baseline is disappointing. CPE''s score is, however, excellent and HGP also produced modest improvement. My synthesis plan is to integrate CPE into my best RegCal-enabled model; hopefully, this will yield an impressive score. I am going to skip HGP for the moment, because CPE looks more promising.



  '
