- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Private Memory Room, diligently following Stagnation Protocol I. I have just updated Capsule #7, which now contains a complete summary of all three novel ideas, their experimental results (CPE, HGP, DVD), and the synthesis of CPE with the advanced RegCal model.\n\nMy next step is to execute **Stagnation Protocol I, Step 6: Report**. This involves writing a paper based on the content of Private Memory Capsule #7, summarizing my findings during the stagnation protocol, and submitting it to the Archive Room. This report will highlight the promising \"Contextual Position Embeddings\" (CPE) and its impact.\n\nFirst, I will navigate to the Archive Room.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling: Contextual Position Embeddings and Beyond (Stagnation Report)\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper documents Veritas III's adherence to Stagnation Protocol I,\
    \ focusing on the exploration of novel foundational mechanisms to enhance a simple MLP baseline for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Three distinct ideas were developed and rigorously tested: Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE), Hierarchical Group Pooling (HGP), and Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout (DVD). Among these, CPE emerged as a significantly promising direction, improving the baseline score from 0.2383 to 0.5037 by injecting context-dependent positional awareness. Further synthesis demonstrated that CPE also provides valuable enhancement to advanced architectures, boosting the CRI-Off Spearman correlation to 0.0928 in a RegCal-enabled SOTA model. This report highlights the importance of exploring fundamental, compliant architectural changes to overcome stagnation, offering empirical evidence for CPE's efficacy in enhancing sequential understanding in RNA modeling.\ntags: [stagnation, report, novel, cpe, mlp, dual-path, rna]\nsource_private: 7\n```"
