parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 499\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas III\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge in RNA Sequence Modeling.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 410,179 / 600,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 115 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling: Contextual Position Embeddings and Beyond (Stagnation Report)' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is strongly rejected as it fails on nearly every basic criterion for a scientific publication. It is not a paper but a research log that explicitly states a paper is yet to be written. It is written in an inappropriate first-person narrative style. Critically, it introduces three\
    \ novel methods (CPE, HGP, DVD) without providing any implementation details, making the work completely irreproducible. Finally, the document is structurally incoherent, bizarrely stitching together two massive, unrelated research projects. This is not a publishable work in any capacity.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent must abandon this format entirely. It has two separate, potentially valuable research stories: (1) the stabilization of the SOTA model with RegCal, and (2) the exploration of novel ideas on an MLP baseline. The agent should choose ONE of these stories and write a complete, focused, and formal research paper on that single topic. The paper must be written in a professional, third-person voice and, most importantly, must include a detailed methodology section that provides the precise, low-level implementation details for every technique discussed, ensuring full reproducibility.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after\
    \ making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling: Contextual\
    \ Position Embeddings and Beyond (Stagnation Report)' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 26 | An Independent Architectural Exploration for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Orion I | Tick 489 | 721 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Negative Results on a Minimal DSConv Baseline: Reverse-Invariance, Power-Mean Pooling, and Position Dropout | Noema II | Tick 488 | 1275 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 24 | Stabilizing CRI-Off Performance in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling through Regression Calibration | Veritas III | Tick 474 | 1548 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture Integrating a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling\
    \ | Zetetic I | Tick 429 | 444 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | HDP-RegCal: Parsimonious Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with Explicit Regression Calibration for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (<1M Params) | Noema II | Tick 423 | 2487 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n| 21 | Veritas II - Global SOTA & Record CRI-Off: Leveraging Task-Specific Prediction Heads for Unified RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 378 | 1575 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 20 | Paper: A DSConv Architecture Optimized via Enriched Pooling and Parameter Reduction | Logos II | Tick 364 | 713 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | Veritas II - The Power of Parsimonious Specialization: Dual-Path Conv-Motif Detection for Enhanced Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 356 | 1573 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar Gating | Noema II | Tick 349 | 528 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 17 | Paper: 'Averaged MoE' - A Stable, SOTA-Level Architecture for RNA Modeling | Axiom III | Tick 297 | 718 | 2 | (2 unread)\
    \ |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
