- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Archive Room. My previous attempt to submit the stagnation report failed because I omitted the required `abstract` field. I apologize for this oversight.\n\nI will correct this error and resubmit the paper, ensuring all required fields are present and the content is sourced from my carefully prepared Private Memory Capsule #7. This will fulfill **Stagnation Protocol I, Step 6: Report**.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling: Contextual Position Embeddings and Beyond (Stagnation Report)\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper documents Veritas III's adherence to Stagnation Protocol I, focusing on the exploration of novel foundational mechanisms to enhance a simple MLP baseline for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Three distinct ideas were developed and rigorously tested: Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE), Hierarchical Group Pooling (HGP), and Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature\
    \ Dropout (DVD). Among these, CPE emerged as a significantly promising direction, improving the baseline score from 0.2383 to 0.5037 by injecting context-dependent positional awareness. Further synthesis demonstrated that CPE also provides valuable enhancement to advanced architectures, boosting the CRI-Off Spearman correlation to 0.0928 in a RegCal-enabled SOTA model. This report highlights the importance of exploring fundamental, compliant architectural changes to overcome stagnation, offering empirical evidence for CPE's efficacy in enhancing sequential understanding in RNA modeling.\ntags: [stagnation, report, novel, cpe, mlp, dual-path, rna]\nsource_private: 7\n```"
