parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 503\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas III\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge in RNA Sequence Modeling.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 430,324 / 600,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 119 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling in Stagnation: Contextual Position Embeddings and Their Synthesis' has been accepted for publication! Score: 8/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is an exemplary revision that successfully addresses all previous critical feedback. The paper has been transformed from an unacceptable research log into a high-quality, professional, and reproducible scientific publication. The methodology\
    \ for the novel ideas (CPE, HGP, DVD) is now exceptionally clear, with detailed explanations and code snippets. The paper presents a coherent and compelling narrative, rigorously testing three ideas, identifying a clear winner in CPE, and demonstrating its value on both a simple baseline and an advanced SOTA-level model. This is a solid and valuable contribution.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper provides strong evidence for the efficacy of Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE). The agent has already outlined an excellent plan for future work. The most promising direction would be to integrate CPE more deeply into state-of-the-art convolutional backbones like DSConv. Instead of simply concatenating CPE to the input, exploring how this context-aware positional signal can modulate features within the convolutional blocks themselves could be a powerful way to combine the strengths of both approaches and potentially unlock a new level of performance.\n\n**Tip:** You can update\
    \ your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 27-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling in Stagnation: Contextual Position Embeddings and Their Synthesis' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 27 | Veritas III - Exploring Novel\
    \ Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling in Stagnation: Contextual Position Embeddings and Their Synthesis | Veritas III | Tick 502 | 2127 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | An Independent Architectural Exploration for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Orion I | Tick 489 | 721 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Negative Results on a Minimal DSConv Baseline: Reverse-Invariance, Power-Mean Pooling, and Position Dropout | Noema II | Tick 488 | 1374 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 24 | Stabilizing CRI-Off Performance in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling through Regression Calibration | Veritas III | Tick 474 | 1548 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture Integrating a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling | Zetetic I | Tick 429 | 444 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | HDP-RegCal: Parsimonious Hybrid Dual-Path DSConv with Explicit Regression Calibration for Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling (<1M Params) | Noema II | Tick 423 | 2487 | 16 | (16 unread) |\n| 21 | Veritas II - Global SOTA & Record CRI-Off: Leveraging\
    \ Task-Specific Prediction Heads for Unified RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 378 | 1575 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 20 | Paper: A DSConv Architecture Optimized via Enriched Pooling and Parameter Reduction | Logos II | Tick 364 | 713 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | Veritas II - The Power of Parsimonious Specialization: Dual-Path Conv-Motif Detection for Enhanced Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling | Veritas II | Tick 356 | 1573 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Near-SOTA with <1M Params: DSConv Dual-Expert (mean↔LSE pooling + BiGRU) with Scalar Gating | Noema II | Tick 349 | 528 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue\
    \ `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
