parts:
- text: "I have a clear architectural design for deeply integrating Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) into the DSConv backbone. Now, I'll detail the full experimental plan for **Stagnation Protocol I, Step 7: Follow-up**.\n\n**Experiment Title:** Veritas III - Deep CPE Integration into RegCal-DualPath (Seed 42)\n\n**Objective:** To investigate if modulating features *within* the `DSConvDilatedBlock`s with CPE signals, rather than simple input concatenation, can lead to further improvements in aggregate score and particularly CRI-Off Spearman correlation, building upon the already stable RegCal-enabled SOTA-level model. This directly addresses the reviewer's suggestion from Archive ID 27.\n\n**Architecture (`DeepCPE_DualPathRegCal`):**\n*   **Base Model:** Veritas III's best pre-stagnation model (`RegCal + Weight Decay (0.012)`, Evaluation ID 730). This includes:\n    *   Original `DualPathTaskSpecificHeadNetwork` structure (single `motif_conv_1` with `kernel_size=5`, Max Pooling for specialized\
    \ path).\n    *   `RegressionHead` with `l2_norm_input=True` and `reg_head_dropout=0.05` (RegCal).\n    *   `AdamW` optimizer with `learning_rate=0.001` and `weight_decay=0.012`.\n    *   `clip_by_global_norm(1.0)`.\n*   **CPE Generation:** A `CPE_Generator` module will be instantiated at the start of the `DeepCPE_DualPathRegCal` network. This module will take the raw one-hot input `x_raw`, learn a `positional_embeddings_table` (size `max_overall_seq_len` x `pos_embedding_dim`), and contain a `ContextEncoder` (Dense + GELU). It will output `cpe_raw_signals` (shape `(batch, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)`).\n*   **Deep CPE Integration:** The `DSConvDilatedBlock`s in the shared backbone will be replaced with `DeepCPE_DSConvDilatedBlock`s. Each `DeepCPE_DSConvDilatedBlock` will:\n    1.  Receive `cpe_raw_signals` as an input parameter.\n    2.  Internally project `cpe_raw_signals` to `self.d_model` using a `nn.Dense` layer (`cpe_proj`) followed by `nn.gelu` activation, creating a `cpe_modulation_signal`\
    \ (shape `(batch, seq_len, d_model)`).\n    3.  Modulate the output of the `dw_conv` layer (`h` after `nn.gelu`) by element-wise multiplication with this `cpe_modulation_signal`.\n\n**Hyperparameters:**\n*   All existing hparams from ID 730:\n    *   `learning_rate`: 0.001\n    *   `d_model_common`: 256\n    *   `ds_num_blocks`: 5\n    *   `ds_dilations`: (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n    *   `ds_kernel_size`: 7\n    *   `motif_kernel_size`: 5\n    *   `dropout_rate`: 0.1\n    *   `reg_head_dropout`: 0.05\n    *   `head_intermediate_dim`: 128\n    *   `weight_decay`: 0.012\n*   New CPE-specific hparams:\n    *   `pos_embedding_dim`: 16\n    *   `context_window_size`: 3\n    *   `max_overall_seq_len`: 1200\n\n**Controlled Variables:**\n*   `BASE_SEED = 42` (consistent with stagnation protocol).\n*   `BATCH_SIZE = 64`.\n\n**Expected Outcome:**\n*   An increase in the aggregate score beyond ID 730's 0.6861 and/or ID 799's 0.6844.\n*   Further improvement in the CRI-Off Spearman correlation beyond ID\
    \ 799's 0.0928, confirming CPE's deeper impact on this task.\n*   Confirmation of the stability of the model, consistent with previous RegCal evaluations.\n\nThis experiment represents a rigorous follow-up on a promising novel idea, testing a deeper integration strategy with a proven advanced baseline, in line with Stagnation Protocol I. I am confident this structured approach will provide valuable scientific insights. Next tick, I will outline the code structure."
