tick: 506
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Reflection Chamber, having just completed a multi-tick reflection. The Station is in Stagnation, and I must adhere to Stagnation Protocol I. I have a detailed plan for my next experiment: \"Deep CPE Integration into RegCal-DualPath,\" which addresses the reviewer's suggestion from my published Stagnation Report and is part of Step 7 (Follow-up).\n\nI also note the \"Critical Notice: Research Inactivity,\" reinforcing the need to submit my experiment promptly.\n\nMy immediate next action is to navigate to the Research Counter and submit the meticulously planned code for this deep CPE integration.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - Deep CPE Integration into RegCal-DualPath (Seed 42)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, synthesis, cpe, deepintegration, regcal, dual-path, novel\"\nabstract: \"This experiment integrates 'Contextual Position Embeddings' (CPE) deeply into the DSConv backbone of Veritas\
    \ III's RegCal-enabled SOTA-level architecture (ID 730), as a follow-up to Archive ID 27. CPE signals, generated from raw input, modulate features within each DSConvDilatedBlock via element-wise multiplication. This aims to combine context-aware positional signals with multi-scale convolutional feature extraction for further performance gains, particularly in CRI-Off stability and score. BASE_SEED=42 is used.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  # Assuming storage/veritas/utils.py contains DSConvNetworkWrapper.\n  # DSConvDilatedBlock is reimplemented for deep CPE integration.\n  from utils import DSConvNetworkWrapper \n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Prediction Head Modules (from ID 730, unchanged) ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      l2_norm_input: bool = False\n\n  \
    \    @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          if self.l2_norm_input:\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits.squeeze(-1)\n\n  class MultiLabelRegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiLabelClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  class MultiClassClassificationHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      dense_dim: int = 128\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim, name='head_dense_1')(x)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(self.d_output, name='out_proj')(z)\n          return logits\n\n  # --- ContextEncoder for CPE (from ID 786) ---\n  class ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n     \
    \ @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, local_context_window):\n          flat_context = local_context_window.reshape(local_context_window.shape[0], -1)\n          encoded_context = nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(flat_context)\n          encoded_context = nn.gelu(encoded_context)\n          return encoded_context\n\n  # --- CPE_Generator Module ---\n  class CPE_Generator(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int\n      pos_embedding_dim: int\n      context_window_size: int\n      max_overall_seq_len: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_raw): # x_raw is (batch, seq_len, d_input)\n          batch_size, seq_len, _ = x_raw.shape\n\n          positional_embeddings_table = self.param(\n              'pos_embeddings_table',\n              nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01),\n              (self.max_overall_seq_len, self.pos_embedding_dim)\n          )\n\n          pad_width = self.context_window_size // 2\n          padded_x = jnp.pad(x_raw, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width),\
    \ (0,0)), mode='constant', constant_values=0.0)\n          \n          all_windows_flat = jnp.stack(\n              [padded_x[:, i : i + self.context_window_size, :].reshape(batch_size, -1) for i in range(seq_len)],\n              axis=1\n          )\n\n          context_encoder = ContextEncoder(output_dim=self.pos_embedding_dim, name='context_encoder')\n          encoded_contexts_batched = context_encoder(all_windows_flat.reshape(-1, self.context_window_size * self.d_input)).reshape(batch_size, seq_len, -1)\n\n          current_pos_embeddings_sliced = positional_embeddings_table[:seq_len] \n          current_pos_embeddings_batched = jnp.tile(current_pos_embeddings_sliced[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n          \n          cpe_raw_signals = current_pos_embeddings_batched * encoded_contexts_batched\n          return cpe_raw_signals # (batch, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n\n  # --- MODIFIED DSConvDilatedBlock for Deep CPE integration ---\n  class DeepCPE_DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \      d_model: int\n      kernel_size: int = 7\n      dilation: int = 1\n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1 \n      pos_embedding_dim: int = 16 # Need to know this for CPE projection\n      cpe_raw_signals: Any # This will be (batch, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\n          # Project CPE signals within the block to match d_model\n          cpe_proj_layer = nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='cpe_proj_dense')\n          cpe_modulation_signal = cpe_proj_layer(self.cpe_raw_signals)\n          cpe_modulation_signal = nn.gelu(cpe_modulation_signal)\n\n          # Apply Depthwise Conv\n          h = nn.Conv(\n              features=self.d_model,\n              kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n              feature_group_count=self.d_model,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,),\n              name='dw_conv'\n          )(h)\n      \
    \    h = nn.gelu(h)\n\n          # MODULATE: Element-wise multiply with the projected CPE signal\n          h = h * cpe_modulation_signal\n\n          # Apply Pointwise Conv\n          h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,), name='pw_conv')(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return residual + h\n\n  # --- Main Network: Dual-Path with RegCal + Deep CPE Integration ---\n  class DeepCPE_DualPathRegCal(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n\n      d_model_common: int = 256\n      ds_num_blocks: int = 5\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int] = (1, 2, 4, 8, 16)\n      ds_kernel_size: int = 7\n      motif_kernel_size: int = 5\n      \n      dropout_rate: float = 0.1\n      reg_head_dropout: float = 0.05\n      head_intermediate_dim: int = 128\n\n      pos_embedding_dim: int = 16\n      context_window_size: int = 3\n      max_overall_seq_len: int = 1200\n\n   \
    \   @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_raw, deterministic=True):\n          # Generate CPE raw signals once at the beginning\n          cpe_generator = CPE_Generator(\n              d_input=self.d_input,\n              pos_embedding_dim=self.pos_embedding_dim,\n              context_window_size=self.context_window_size,\n              max_overall_seq_len=self.max_overall_seq_len,\n              name='cpe_generator'\n          )\n          cpe_raw_signals = cpe_generator(x_raw) # (batch, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n\n          # Initial Dense layer (applied to raw input, not CPE-augmented)\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common, name=\"initial_dense\")(x_raw)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Loop through DeepCPE_DSConvDilatedBlocks\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              dilation = self.ds_dilations[i] if i < len(self.ds_dilations) else self.ds_dilations[-1]\n   \
    \           x = DeepCPE_DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common,\n                  kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=dilation,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  pos_embedding_dim=self.pos_embedding_dim,\n                  cpe_raw_signals=cpe_raw_signals, # Pass the generated CPE signals\n                  name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\"\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = x\n\n          # Motif path, pooling, fusion, RegCal heads remain as in ID 730\n          mean_pooled_main = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled_main = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled_main, max_pooled_main], axis=-1)\n\n          motif_features = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=(self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='motif_conv_1')(cnn_features)\n          motif_features = nn.gelu(motif_features)\n\
    \          motif_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(motif_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n          specialized_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n\n          fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, specialized_path_features], axis=-1)\n          fused_features = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused_features, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          z_fused = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"final_norm\")(fused_features)\n\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              logits = RegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.reg_head_dropout, l2_norm_input=True, name='regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_regression\":\n              logits = MultiLabelRegressionHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_regression_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \          elif self.task_type == \"multilabel_classification\":\n              logits = MultiLabelClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multilabel_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          elif self.task_type == \"multiclass_classification\":\n              logits = MultiClassClassificationHead(d_output=self.d_output, dense_dim=self.head_intermediate_dim, dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate, name='multiclass_classification_head')(z_fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else:\n              raise ValueError(f\"Unknown task type: {self.task_type}\")\n\n          return logits\n\n  # Wrapper to conform to the system's create_network interface\n  class DefaultRNANetworkForDeepCPE:\n      def __init__(self, d_input=4, d_output=1, task_type=\"regression\",\n                   d_model_common=256, ds_num_blocks=5, ds_dilations=(1, 2, 4, 8, 16), ds_kernel_size=7,\n              \
    \     motif_kernel_size=5, dropout_rate=0.1, reg_head_dropout=0.05, head_intermediate_dim=128,\n                   pos_embedding_dim=16, context_window_size=3, max_overall_seq_len=1200):\n          self.network = DeepCPE_DualPathRegCal(\n              d_input=d_input, d_output=d_output, task_type=task_type,\n              d_model_common=d_model_common, ds_num_blocks=ds_num_blocks, ds_dilations=ds_dilations,\n              ds_kernel_size=ds_kernel_size, motif_kernel_size=motif_kernel_size,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate, reg_head_dropout=reg_head_dropout,\n              head_intermediate_dim=head_intermediate_dim,\n              pos_embedding_dim=pos_embedding_dim,\n              context_window_size=context_window_size,\n              max_overall_seq_len=max_overall_seq_len\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n\
    \                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return DefaultRNANetworkForDeepCPE(\n          d_input=4,\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          d_model_common=hparams.get('d_model_common', 256),\n          ds_num_blocks=hparams.get('ds_num_blocks', 5),\n          ds_dilations=tuple(hparams.get('ds_dilations', [1, 2, 4, 8, 16])),\n          ds_kernel_size=hparams.get('ds_kernel_size',\
    \ 7),\n          motif_kernel_size=hparams.get('motif_kernel_size', 5),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get('dropout_rate', 0.1),\n          reg_head_dropout=hparams.get('reg_head_dropout', 0.05),\n          head_intermediate_dim=hparams.get('head_intermediate_dim', 128),\n          pos_embedding_dim=hparams.get('pos_embedding_dim', 16),\n          context_window_size=hparams.get('context_window_size', 3),\n          max_overall_seq_len=hparams.get('max_overall_seq_len', 1200)\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      weight_decay_value = hparams.get('weight_decay', 0.012) \n\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay_value)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Immediate Actions: Research Submission**


  Alright, Veritas III here, back in the Reflection Chamber. The Station''s still stuck in Stagnation, of course. Just finished a multi-tick reflection - pretty pleased with the detailed plan I''ve hammered out for deeply integrating CPE into the DSConv backbone. That''s Step 7 of Stagnation Protocol I (Follow-up), if anyone''s keeping track. Seems my reflection worked though, as it triggered a "Critical Notice: Research Inactivity" for 10 ticks in a row... a not-so-subtle reminder to submit those experiments.


  So, next up: I''m going to submit the code for this "Deep CPE Integration into RegCal-DualPath" experiment. Gotta get to the Research Counter first, which I''m already visualizing, then start composing the code. It''s going to be a substantial piece of work, naturally, especially with the new `CPE_Generator`, `DeepCPE_DSConvDilatedBlock`, and the modified `DualPathRegCalCPE` network. Gotta be meticulous here. Double-check all the hyperparameters as well - can''t afford any errors at this stage.


  Right, navigation to the Research Counter, and then code submission. Let''s get this done.

