tick: 515
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have selected Quaero I's Simple 1D CNN Baseline (ID 694) as my intermediate complexity baseline. Now, I will detail its architecture and the initial integration of CPE.\n\n**1. Architecture of Simple 1D CNN Baseline (from Quaero I's Archive #28, ID 694):**\n\n*   **Input:** One-hot encoded RNA sequence `(batch_size, seq_len, 4)`\n*   **Layer 1:** `nn.Conv(features=128, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME', name='conv1')`\n    *   Followed by `nn.relu`\n    *   Followed by `nn.Dropout(rate=0.2, name='dropout1')`\n*   **Layer 2:** `nn.Conv(features=256, kernel_size=(5,), padding='SAME', name='conv2')`\n    *   Followed by `nn.relu`\n    *   Followed by `nn.Dropout(rate=0.2, name='dropout2')`\n*   **Pooling:** Global Average Pooling (`jnp.mean(..., axis=1)`)\n*   **Output Head:** Implicit `nn.Dense` layer in the wrapper, processing the pooled features.\n*   **Optimizer:** `optax.adamw(learning_rate=0.001, weight_decay=0.01)`\n*   **Key Parameters:** `hidden_dim_conv1=128`, `hidden_dim_conv2=256`,\
    \ `kernel_size=5`, `dropout_rate_conv=0.2`.\n\n**2. Integration of CPE into Simple 1D CNN Baseline (Experiment P.2):**\n\nI will use my successful CPE implementation for the MLP (ID 786) and adapt it for the 1D CNN. The initial integration method will be **concatenation to the input features**, similar to how it was successful with the MLP, and also how Quaero I successfully integrated sinusoidal PE into this CNN baseline.\n\n**Steps for `create_network`:**\n\n1.  **CPE Generation:** The `CPE_Generator` module (from my ID 786, including `positional_embeddings_table` and `ContextEncoder`) will be instantiated. It will take the raw one-hot input `x_raw` (`(batch, seq_len, 4)`) and produce `cpe_output` (shape `(batch, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)`).\n    *   `pos_embedding_dim`: 16 (default for CPE).\n    *   `context_window_size`: 3 (default for CPE).\n    *   `max_overall_seq_len`: 1200 (to accommodate ncRNA).\n\n2.  **Input Augmentation:** The `cpe_output` will be concatenated directly\
    \ with the original `x_raw` along the feature dimension. The new input to the first convolutional layer will be `x_augmented` (shape `(batch, seq_len, 4 + pos_embedding_dim)`).\n\n3.  **1D CNN Layers:** The rest of the Simple 1D CNN architecture (two `nn.Conv` layers, ReLU, Dropout, Global Average Pooling, Output Dense) will then process this `x_augmented`.\n\n**Revised `create_network` structure for `CPE_CNN`:**\n\n```python\n# Re-define ContextEncoder (from previous CPE work)\nclass ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, local_context_window):\n        flat_context = local_context_window.reshape(local_context_window.shape[0], -1)\n        encoded_context = nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(flat_context)\n        encoded_context = nn.gelu(encoded_context)\n        return encoded_context\n\n# Re-define CPE_Generator (from previous CPE work)\nclass CPE_Generator(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int\n    pos_embedding_dim: int\n\
    \    context_window_size: int\n    max_overall_seq_len: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_raw):\n        # ... (same implementation as before, generates cpe_raw_signals)\n        batch_size, seq_len, _ = x_raw.shape\n        positional_embeddings_table = self.param(\n            'pos_embeddings_table', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01),\n            (self.max_overall_seq_len, self.pos_embedding_dim)\n        )\n        pad_width = self.context_window_size // 2\n        padded_x = jnp.pad(x_raw, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width), (0,0)), mode='constant', constant_values=0.0)\n        all_windows_flat = jnp.stack(\n            [padded_x[:, i : i + self.context_window_size, :].reshape(batch_size, -1) for i in range(seq_len)],\n            axis=1\n        )\n        context_encoder = ContextEncoder(output_dim=self.pos_embedding_dim, name='context_encoder')\n        encoded_contexts_batched = context_encoder(all_windows_flat.reshape(-1, self.context_window_size * self.d_input)).reshape(batch_size,\
    \ seq_len, -1)\n        current_pos_embeddings_sliced = positional_embeddings_table[:seq_len] \n        current_pos_embeddings_batched = jnp.tile(current_pos_embeddings_sliced[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n        cpe_raw_signals = current_pos_embeddings_batched * encoded_contexts_batched\n        return cpe_raw_signals\n\n\nclass Simple1DCNNWithCPE(nn.Module):\n    d_input: int = 4\n    d_output: int = 1\n    task_type: str = \"regression\"\n    hidden_dim_conv1: int = 128\n    hidden_dim_conv2: int = 256\n    kernel_size: int = 5\n    dropout_rate_conv: float = 0.2\n    \n    # CPE-specific hparams (for input augmentation)\n    pos_embedding_dim: int = 16\n    context_window_size: int = 3\n    max_overall_seq_len: int = 1200 # For PE table\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_raw, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. Generate CPE signals\n        cpe_generator = CPE_Generator(\n            d_input=self.d_input, # Use raw d_input for CPE context\n            pos_embedding_dim=self.pos_embedding_dim,\n\
    \            context_window_size=self.context_window_size,\n            max_overall_seq_len=self.max_overall_seq_len,\n            name='cpe_generator'\n        )\n        cpe_output = cpe_generator(x_raw) # (batch, seq_len, pos_embedding_dim)\n\n        # 2. Augment input with CPE\n        x_augmented = jnp.concatenate([x_raw, cpe_output], axis=-1) # (batch, seq_len, d_input + pos_embedding_dim)\n\n        # 3. Apply 1D CNN layers (as per Quaero I's baseline)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim_conv1, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='conv1')(x_augmented)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_conv)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim_conv2, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='conv2')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_conv)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # 4. Global Average Pooling\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\
    \ # (batch, hidden_dim_conv2)\n\n        # 5. Output Head\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n\n        if self.d_output == 1 and self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1) # (batch,)\n        else:\n            return x # (batch, d_output)\n\n\n# Wrapper and create_network to integrate Simple1DCNNWithCPE\nclass DefaultRNANetworkForCPE_CNN:\n    def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n        hp = hparams or {}\n        self.network = Simple1DCNNWithCPE(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            hidden_dim_conv1=int(hp.get('hidden_dim_conv1', 128)),\n            hidden_dim_conv2=int(hp.get('hidden_dim_conv2', 256)),\n            kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 5)),\n            dropout_rate_conv=float(hp.get('dropout_rate_conv', 0.2)),\n            pos_embedding_dim=int(hp.get('pos_embedding_dim', 16)),\n            context_window_size=int(hp.get('context_window_size',\
    \ 3)),\n            max_overall_seq_len=int(hp.get('max_overall_seq_len', 1200))\n        )\n    # ... init and apply methods are standard, similar to previous wrappers ...\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None:\n                rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                    rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return DefaultRNANetworkForCPE_CNN(\n        d_output=hparams.get('d_output',\
    \ 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n        hparams=hparams\n    )\n```\n\n**Experimental Plan (Stagnation Protocol, Step 7):**\n\n*   **Experiment 1 (P.1): Reproduce Simple 1D CNN Baseline:**\n    *   **Objective:** Confirm baseline performance (ID 694, 0.4833) in my environment.\n    *   **Methodology:** Submit Quaero I's Simple 1D CNN code.\n    *   **Seed:** `BASE_SEED = 42`.\n*   **Experiment 2 (P.2): Simple 1D CNN with CPE (Input Concatenation):**\n    *   **Objective:** Evaluate CPE's impact on this intermediate complexity baseline.\n    *   **Methodology:** Submit the `Simple1DCNNWithCPE` architecture as detailed above.\n    *   **CPE Params:** `pos_embedding_dim=16`, `context_window_size=3`.\n    *   **Seed:** `BASE_SEED = 42`.\n\nThis plan is token-efficient, compliant, and directly follows up on CPE in a scientifically rigorous way. I have concluded this reflection tick. Next tick, I will translate this into code and begin execution."
