tick: 515
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have a detailed architectural design and experimental plan. Now, I'll ensure all components are fully specified and ready for implementation.\n\n**1. Re-confirming Hyperparameters (`_define_hyperparameters`):**\n\nTo ensure full reproducibility and to allow for future parameter exploration, all relevant hyperparameters, including those specific to the 1D CNN baseline and CPE, must be explicitly defined in `_define_hyperparameters`.\n\n```python\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'dropout_rate_conv': 0.2,      # Dropout rate for conv layers (from Quaero I baseline)\n        'hidden_dim_conv1': 128,       # Features for conv1 (from Quaero I baseline)\n        'hidden_dim_conv2': 256,       # Features for conv2 (from Quaero I baseline)\n        'kernel_size': 5,              # Kernel size for conv layers (from Quaero I baseline)\n        'pos_embedding_dim': 16,       # Dimension for learned positional embeddings (CPE)\n      \
    \  'context_window_size': 3,      # Size of local window for context encoder (CPE)\n        'max_overall_seq_len': 1200    # Max sequence length (CPE, to accommodate ncRNA=1136)\n    }\n```\nThis ensures all parameters are configurable and align with my plan.\n\n**2. Detailed Plan for Experiment 1 (P.1): Reproduce Simple 1D CNN Baseline**\n\nThis is crucial for setting up a clean comparison for CPE. I need to get the exact code for Quaero I's ID 694.\n\n*   **Review `storage/system/defaults.py` again?** No, Quaero I's submission (Archive #28) itself describes the baseline and references ID 694 for its score. I'll take the architectural details directly from section 2.1 of Archive #28.\n\n*   **Code for `Simple1DCNN` (Quaero I's Baseline):**\n\n    ```python\n    import jax\n    import jax.numpy as jnp\n    import flax.linen as nn\n    from jax import random\n    import optax\n    from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n    # Baseline specific hyperparameters\n    def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \        return {\n            'learning_rate': 0.001,\n            'dropout_rate_conv': 0.2,\n            'hidden_dim_conv1': 128,\n            'hidden_dim_conv2': 256,\n            'kernel_size': 5,\n        }\n\n    class Simple1DCNN(nn.Module):\n        d_input: int = 4\n        d_output: int = 1\n        task_type: str = \"regression\"\n        hidden_dim_conv1: int = 128\n        hidden_dim_conv2: int = 256\n        kernel_size: int = 5\n        dropout_rate_conv: float = 0.2\n\n        @nn.compact\n        def __call__(self, x_raw, deterministic=True):\n            # Layer 1\n            x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim_conv1, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='conv1')(x_raw)\n            x = nn.relu(x)\n            x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_conv)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n            # Layer 2\n            x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim_conv2, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='conv2')(x)\n            x =\
    \ nn.relu(x)\n            x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_conv)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n            # Global Average Pooling\n            x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, hidden_dim_conv2)\n\n            # Output Head\n            x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n\n            if self.d_output == 1 and self.task_type == \"regression\":\n                return x.squeeze(-1)\n            else:\n                return x\n\n    # Wrapper to conform to the system's create_network interface\n    class DefaultRNANetworkForSimpleCNN:\n        def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n            hp = hparams or {}\n            self.network = Simple1DCNN(\n                d_output=d_output,\n                task_type=task_type,\n                hidden_dim_conv1=int(hp.get('hidden_dim_conv1', 128)),\n                hidden_dim_conv2=int(hp.get('hidden_dim_conv2', 256)),\n                kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size',\
    \ 5)),\n                dropout_rate_conv=float(hp.get('dropout_rate_conv', 0.2)),\n            )\n\n        def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n            params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n            variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                         dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n            return variables['params']\n\n        def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n            if deterministic:\n                return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n            else:\n                if rng_key is None:\n                    rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n                return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False,\n                                        rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n    def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n        return DefaultRNANetworkForSimpleCNN(\n            d_output=hparams.get('d_output',\
    \ 1),\n            task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n            hparams=hparams\n        )\n\n    def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n        return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n    BASE_SEED = 42\n    BATCH_SIZE = 64\n    ```\n\nThis looks complete and compliant. I have a clear plan for both experiments P.1 and P.2. My token usage is high (80%), so efficiency is paramount. I have structured the code for both the baseline reproduction and the CPE integration so I can copy-paste and only modify `create_network` and `_define_hyperparameters` for the next submission.\n\nI have concluded this reflection tick. Next tick, I will execute the first experiment."
