parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Reflection Chamber, having just completed a multi-tick reflection. The Station is in Stagnation, and I must adhere to Stagnation Protocol I. I have a detailed plan for my next experiment series, focusing on \"Contextual Position Embeddings\" (CPE) with Quaero I's Simple 1D CNN Baseline.\n\nI have received a token budget PRE-WARNING (81% used). I will continue to be token-efficient.\n\nMy immediate next action is to navigate to the Research Counter and submit the code for **Experiment P.1: Reproduce Simple 1D CNN Baseline**. This is the first step in my new research direction under Step 7 (Follow-up).\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - SP: Reproduce Simple 1D CNN Baseline (ID 694, Seed 42)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, baseline, reproduction, cnn, simple\"\nabstract: \"This submission reproduces Quaero I's Simple 1D CNN Baseline (Evaluation ID 694, score 0.4833) as part of Stagnation Protocol\
    \ I, Step 7. This establishes a consistent intermediate complexity baseline for Veritas III's subsequent CPE experiments. BASE_SEED=42 is explicitly set for reproducibility.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # Baseline specific hyperparameters\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'dropout_rate_conv': 0.2,\n          'hidden_dim_conv1': 128,\n          'hidden_dim_conv2': 256,\n          'kernel_size': 5,\n      }\n\n  class Simple1DCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_input: int = 4\n      d_output: int = 1\n      task_type: str = \"regression\"\n      hidden_dim_conv1: int = 128\n      hidden_dim_conv2: int = 256\n      kernel_size: int = 5\n      dropout_rate_conv: float = 0.2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_raw, deterministic=True):\n          # Layer 1\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim_conv1,\
    \ kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='conv1')(x_raw)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_conv)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Layer 2\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.hidden_dim_conv2, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', name='conv2')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate_conv)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          # Global Average Pooling\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1) # (batch, hidden_dim_conv2)\n\n          # Output Head\n          x = nn.Dense(self.d_output)(x) # (batch, d_output)\n\n          if self.d_output == 1 and self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  # Wrapper to conform to the system's create_network interface\n  class DefaultRNANetworkForSimpleCNN:\n      def __init__(self, d_output=1, task_type='regression', hparams: Dict[str, Any] = None):\n          hp\
    \ = hparams or {}\n          self.network = Simple1DCNN(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim_conv1=int(hp.get('hidden_dim_conv1', 128)),\n              hidden_dim_conv2=int(hp.get('hidden_dim_conv2', 256)),\n              kernel_size=int(hp.get('kernel_size', 5)),\n              dropout_rate_conv=float(hp.get('dropout_rate_conv', 0.2)),\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                       dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x_raw, deterministic=True, rng_key=None): # x_raw parameter name for consistency\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x_raw, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None:\n\
    \                  rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x_raw, deterministic=False,\n                                      rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return DefaultRNANetworkForSimpleCNN(\n          d_output=hparams.get('d_output', 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get('task_type', 'regression'),\n          hparams=hparams\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64\n```"
