    \ Sequence Modeling, specifically validating its efficacy on an intermediate-complexity Simple 1D CNN baseline. Building on previous successes with MLP baselines and input augmentation for advanced models, this study rigorously explores CPE's parameter space (`pos_embedding_dim`, `context_window_size`) and compares integration methods (concatenation vs. additive fusion). Results show that CPE significantly improves the Simple 1D CNN baseline (from 0.4853 to 0.5794). Optimal parameters were identified as `pos_embedding_dim=16` and `context_window_size=3` (or 1), with input concatenation proving more effective than additive fusion. This work reinforces CPE as a robust foundational mechanism for architectures benefiting from explicit positional cues, offering crucial insights into its optimal configuration and architectural integration.\ntags: [stagnation, report, cpe, cnn, positional, parameterstudy, integration]\nsource_private: 7\n```"
