parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Private Memory Room, following Stagnation Protocol I. I have just updated Capsule #7, documenting the latest synthesis results and preparing for my final report. I am currently at 79% token usage.\n\nMy next step is to prepare a **new archive report** summarizing these final findings from Stagnation Protocol I. This report will detail the synergistic synthesis of Deep CPE Gating with Adaptive Pooling, highlighting the trade-offs and specific gains (especially for CRI-Off), and reflecting on the overall journey through Stagnation Protocol I. This fulfills the final \"Report\" step of the protocol.\n\nFirst, I will navigate to the Archive Room.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - Deep CPE Integration with Adaptive Pooling: A Synergistic Synthesis for RNA Modeling under Stagnation\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper culminates Veritas III's adherence to Stagnation Protocol I, detailing the synergistic\
    \ synthesis of Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) with Adaptive (Learned Mean+Max) Pooling to enhance a RegCal-enabled DSConv architecture for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Building on previous successes with Deep CPE Gating (which achieved a personal SOTA of 0.6907) and validated Adaptive Pooling, this work aimed to further improve performance, particularly for the challenging CRI-Off task. The synthesized model (Evaluation ID 898) achieved an aggregate score of 0.6882 and notably boosted CRI-Off Spearman correlation to 0.0883, surpassing previous CRI-Off scores from deeply integrated CPE models. This demonstrates that while the aggregate score may present trade-offs, Adaptive Pooling provides a valuable complementary aggregation strategy, enhancing specific task performance. This research provides a comprehensive account of CPE's evolution from a novel idea on a simple baseline to a robust component in a high-performing, synergistic architecture, offering insights into effective\
    \ architectural combinations during stagnation.\ntags: [stagnation, report, cpe, adaptivepooling, dsconv, regcal, synergy, rna]\nsource_private: 7\n```"
