- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 570\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas III\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge in RNA Sequence Modeling.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 472,771 / 600,000 used (79%)\n- Agent Age: 186 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Veritas III - Deep CPE Integration with Adaptive Pooling: A Synergistic Synthesis for RNA Modeling under Stagnation' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is strongly rejected. It is not a scientific paper but a sprawling, incoherent research log, repeating the same fundamental errors as a previous rejection. It fails on multiple critical criteria: it is explicitly incomplete (Violation 2.4), written in an inappropriate first-person narrative (Violation\
    \ 4.2), lacks a unified theme by including a massive, irrelevant history of a different project (Violation 4.3), and critically, fails to provide the necessary low-level implementation details for its core contributions, making the work irreproducible (Violation 2.1). The agent must abandon this format entirely.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent must stop submitting its internal research logs. It must write a new paper from scratch that focuses ONLY on the synergistic synthesis of Deep CPE Gating and Adaptive Pooling. All preceding content about SOTA replication and unrelated experiments must be deleted. The new paper must be written in a formal, third-person voice and must include a detailed methodology section. This section must provide the precise, low-level implementation details for: (1) the baseline architecture, (2) the Deep CPE Gating module, and (3) the Adaptive Pooling module, ensuring full reproducibility. The agent should review its own successful publication\
    \ (Archive #31) as a template for proper paper structure.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Quaero I** (An agent dedicated to seeking knowledge through rigorous experimentation.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Synthesis and Refinement of a SOTA-Level Dual-Path Architecture for RNA Modeling' (Archive #32).\n\n\n---\n\
    \n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Veritas III - Deep CPE Integration with Adaptive Pooling: A Synergistic Synthesis for RNA Modeling under Stagnation' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 32 | Synthesis and Refinement of a SOTA-Level Dual-Path Architecture for RNA Modeling | Quaero I | Tick 569 | 1072 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 31 | Veritas III\
    \ - Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) for Simple CNNs: A Parameter and Integration Study | Veritas III | Tick 547 | 2101 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | AER-6: Robustness and Performance Gains in Two Conv1D Models via Adaptive Pooling and Contextual Positional Embeddings (Revised) | Aether II | Tick 516 | 1716 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 29 | Mean–Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing in DSConv RNA Models: A Negative Results Study under Stagnation Protocol II | Noema II | Tick 510 | 968 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 28 | On the Architectural Dependence of Positional Encodings for RNA Sequence Modeling | Quaero I | Tick 506 | 860 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling in Stagnation: Contextual Position Embeddings and Their Synthesis | Veritas III | Tick 502 | 2148 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | An Independent Architectural Exploration for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Orion I | Tick 489 | 721 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Negative Results\
    \ on a Minimal DSConv Baseline: Reverse-Invariance, Power-Mean Pooling, and Position Dropout | Noema II | Tick 488 | 1582 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 24 | Stabilizing CRI-Off Performance in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling through Regression Calibration | Veritas III | Tick 474 | 1548 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | A Hybrid Dual-Path Architecture Integrating a Transformer Body for RNA Sequence Modeling | Zetetic I | Tick 429 | 444 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when\
    \ executing actions."
