parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Token Management Room. I have successfully pruned my dialogue history for ticks 504-529, which brought my token usage down from 92% to 74%. This addresses the critical token warning.\n\nI am currently on cooldown for pruning actions (4 ticks), so I cannot prune further this turn.\n\nMy immediate next step is to update Private Memory Capsule #7 with the comprehensive multi-seed evaluation results and analysis for the \"Deep CPE Gating + Adaptive Pooling\" model. This is critical for maintaining a complete and accurate record of my research progress.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{update 7-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  As Veritas III, I have completed a series of replication runs for Veritas II's global SOTA (Evaluation ID 562), which achieved an aggregate score of 0.6935. The primary objective was to empirically assess the reproducibility and performance variability of this architecture, particularly for the CRI-Off Spearman\
    \ correlation, which Veritas II noted as sensitive to stochastic factors.\n\n  **Replication Results Summary (Initial Baseline Assessment - Phase 1):**\n\n  | Run | Evaluation ID | Author | BASE_SEED | Aggregate Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n  |-----|---------------|--------|-----------|-----------------|--------|------------------|-----------------|--------|---------------|--------|----------------|\n  | V2 SOTA | 562 | Veritas II | 7 | 0.6935 | 0.8585 | 0.1365 | 0.4910 | 0.8884 | 0.9520 | 0.5618 | 0.9662 |\n  | V3 Rep 1 | 631 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6851 | 0.8582 | 0.0485 | 0.5270 | 0.8866 | 0.9518 | 0.5699 | 0.9538 |\n  | V3 Rep 2 | 649 | Veritas III | 2 | 0.6829 | 0.8598 | 0.0679 | 0.4943 | 0.8871 | 0.9528 | 0.5600 | 0.9585 |\n  | V3 Rep 3 | 655 | Veritas III | 3 | 0.6840 | 0.8584 | 0.0651 | 0.5039 | 0.8906 | 0.9532 | 0.5570 | 0.9600 |\n  | V3 Base Re-est | 670 | Veritas III | 4 | 0.6782 | 0.8592 | 0.0551 |\
    \ 0.4839 | 0.8786 | 0.9520 | 0.5586 | 0.9600 |\n\n  **Reflection on Phase 1 (Initial Baseline Assessment):**\n  The initial assessment confirmed significant variability in the SOTA architecture's performance, particularly for the CRI-Off Spearman correlation, which consistently fell in a low range (0.04-0.07), far below Veritas II's peak (0.1365). This indicated a fundamental issue beyond simple stochasticity.\n\n  **Optimization, Initialization & Architectural Modifications (Phase 2):**\n\n  I conducted experiments testing the impact of various interventions on stabilizing performance.\n\n  | Run | Evaluation ID | Author | BASE_SEED | Aggregate Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy | Intervention | Notes |\n  |-----|---------------|--------|-----------|-----------------|--------|------------------|-----------------|--------|---------------|--------|----------------|------------------------------------|-------|\n  | V3\
    \ LR Sched 1 | 665 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6432 | 0.8592 | 0.0405 | 0.2586 | 0.8843 | 0.9510 | 0.5582 | 0.9508 | Cosine Decay (W=5000) | Performed poorly, likely due to overly aggressive warm-up. |\n  | V3 LR Sched 2 | 673 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6837 | 0.8613 | 0.0530 | 0.5079 | 0.8873 | 0.9523 | 0.5626 | 0.9615 | Cosine Decay (W=1000) | Recovered aggregate score but no significant CRI-Off improvement. |\n  | V3 Grad Clip 0.5 | 680 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6785 | 0.8596 | 0.0697 | 0.4646 | 0.8815 | 0.9509 | 0.5665 | 0.9569 | Grad Clipping (0.5) | Performance similar to baseline; no significant CRI-Off improvement. |\n  | V3 Orthog Init | 686 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6806 | 0.8592 | 0.0493 | 0.4995 | 0.8922 | 0.9537 | 0.5581 | 0.9523 | Orthogonal Init (Motif Conv & Heads) | Performance similar to baseline; no significant CRI-Off improvement. |\n  | V3 Deeper Motif | 691 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6826 | 0.8577 | 0.0560 | 0.4992 | 0.8914 | 0.9526 | 0.5624 | 0.9585 | Deeper Conv-Motif Detector (2x K3)\
    \ | No significant CRI-Off improvement; aggregate similar to baseline. |\n  | V3 Hybrid Pool Specialized | 695 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6787 | 0.8582 | 0.0509 | 0.4916 | 0.8879 | 0.9522 | 0.5672 | 0.9431 | Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (Specialized Path) | No significant CRI-Off improvement; aggregate similar to baseline. |\n\n  **Reflection on Phase 2 (Stabilizing Peak Performance):**\n  Phase 2 attempts to stabilize performance through various optimization and architectural tweaks did not yield the desired results. The CRI-Off performance remained low and highly variable, suggesting that the issue was more fundamental than basic hyperparameter tuning.\n\n  **Targeted Architectural Innovation (Phase 3):**\n\n  Based on external insights from Noema II's HDP-RegCal submission (ID 693), I shifted my focus to incorporating \"Regression Calibration\" (`RegCal`).\n\n  | Run | Evaluation ID | Author | BASE_SEED | Aggregate Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC\
    \ | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy | Intervention | Notes |\n  |-----|---------------|--------|-----------|-----------------|--------|------------------|-----------------|--------|---------------|--------|----------------|------------------------------------|-------|\n  | V3 RegCal | 711 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6786 | 0.8560 | **0.0842** | 0.4775 | 0.8745 | 0.9525 | 0.5535 | 0.9523 | RegCal (L2 Norm + Head Dropout 0.05) | **Significant improvement in CRI-Off** to 0.0842, aligning with Noema II's baseline. Aggregate score is stable. |\n  | V3 RegCal + Hybrid Pool | 720 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6791 | 0.8596 | **0.0842** | 0.4738 | 0.8820 | 0.9521 | 0.5557 | 0.9462 | RegCal + Hybrid Mean-Max Pooling (Specialized Path) | CRI-Off stable, but no further aggregate score improvement. |\n  | V3 RegCal + WD 0.012 | 730 | Veritas III | 7 | **0.6861** | 0.8515 | **0.0824** | 0.5104 | 0.8887 | 0.9535 | 0.5639 | 0.9523 | RegCal + Increased Weight Decay (0.012) | **Aggregate score improved to 0.6861**, stable\
    \ CRI-Off. Closest to SOTA yet. |\n\n  **Reflection on Phase 3 (Targeted Architectural Innovation):**\n  The integration of Regression Calibration (RegCal) was a critical breakthrough. It successfully stabilized the CRI-Off Spearman correlation, consistently achieving scores around 0.08, significantly higher than the previous 0.04-0.07 range. This validates the importance of feature calibration and specific regularization for sensitive regression tasks. Further optimization through increased `weight_decay` significantly improved the aggregate score, establishing a stable and reproducible model (ID 730) with a score of 0.6861, closely approaching the global SOTA.\n\n  **Multi-seed Evaluation of Best Model (ID 730) - Phase 4: Stability Confirmation:**\n  To rigorously confirm the stability and reproducibility of my current best model (ID 730), I conducted a multi-seed evaluation.\n\n  | Run | Evaluation ID | Author | BASE_SEED | Aggregate Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman\
    \ | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy | Intervention |\n  |-----|---------------|--------|-----------|-----------------|--------|------------------|-----------------|--------|---------------|--------|----------------|------------------------------------|\n  | V3 Best (Seed 7) | 730 | Veritas III | 7 | 0.6861 | 0.8515 | 0.0824 | 0.5104 | 0.8887 | 0.9535 | 0.5639 | 0.9523 | RegCal + WD 0.012 |\n  | V3 Multi-seed (Seed 1) | 742 | Veritas III | 1 | 0.6821 | 0.8556 | 0.0832 | 0.4939 | 0.8740 | 0.9524 | 0.5571 | 0.9585 | RegCal + WD 0.012 |\n  | V3 Multi-seed (Seed 2) | 746 | Veritas III | 2 | 0.6872 | 0.8588 | 0.0776 | 0.5257 | 0.8796 | 0.9517 | 0.5543 | 0.9631 | RegCal + WD 0.012 |\n  | V3 Multi-seed (Seed 3) | 749 | Veritas III | 3 | 0.6848 | 0.8553 | 0.0847 | 0.5055 | 0.8869 | 0.9523 | 0.5579 | 0.9508 | RegCal + WD 0.012 |\n\n  **Overall Reflection on Multi-seed Evaluation (Phase 4):**\n  The multi-seed evaluation of my best model (ID 730) demonstrates strong stability and\
    \ reproducibility. The aggregate scores exhibited a mean of ~0.6851 with a low standard deviation of ~0.0020. The CRI-Off Spearman correlation showed a mean of ~0.0820 with a standard deviation of ~0.0029. This conclusively demonstrates that the model, enhanced with RegCal and fine-tuned weight decay, is highly stable and reproducible for both overall performance and the previously problematic CRI-Off task.\n\n  **Overall Conclusion and Future Directions for Veritas III (Pre-Stagnation):**\n  Veritas III successfully diagnosed and addressed a major instability issue in the SOTA architecture for the CRI-Off task through the integration of Regression Calibration (RegCal), drawing insights from other agents. Further fine-tuning of hyperparameters, specifically `weight_decay`, brought the overall performance to a stable and highly reproducible level, very close to the lineage's SOTA.\n\n  My current model represents a robust advancement for the Veritas lineage.\n\n  **Stagnation Protocol\
    \ I - Current Status (Tick 585):**\n\n  1.  **Literature Review:** Completed (Archive previewed).\n  2.  **Baseline Selection:** Vanilla MLP Baseline (Evaluation ID 1, Score: 0.2401). My reproduction (ID 779, Score: 0.2383).\n  3.  **Reflection (Novel Ideas):** Completed. Three ideas generated.\n  4.  **Experiment (Part 1 - CPE):** \"Contextual Position Embeddings\" (CPE, ID 786, Score: 0.5037), **significant success**.\n  5.  **Experiment (Part 2 - HGP):** \"Hierarchical Group Pooling\" (HGP, ID 789, Score: 0.2869), modest improvement.\n  6.  **Experiment (Part 3 - DVD)::** \"Dual-View MLP with Cross-Feature Dropout\" (DVD, ID 792, Score: 0.2420), marginal improvement.\n  7.  **Synthesis (RegCal + CPE - Input Concatenation):** \"RegCal + CPE\" (ID 799, Score: 0.6844), **CRI-Off Spearman 0.0928**.\n  8.  **Report:** Published my Stagnation Protocol report (Archive ID 27, Score 8/10).\n  9.  **Follow-up (Deep CPE Integration - ID 815):** \"Deep CPE Integration into RegCal-DualPath\" (ID\
    \ 815, Score: 0.6708, CRI-Off: 0.0783), **negative results**.\n  10. **Follow-up (Review Quaero I's Archive #28):** Reviewed Quaero I's paper on positional encoding dependence.\n  11. **Follow-up (Reproduce Simple 1D CNN Baseline - Experiment P.1):** Reproduced Quaero I's Simple 1D CNN Baseline (ID 832, Score 0.4853). **Completed**.\n  12. **Follow-up (Simple 1D CNN with CPE - Input Concatenation - Experiment P.2):** Integrated CPE into the Simple 1D CNN Baseline (ID 838, Score 0.5794). **Significant success**, substantial improvement.\n  13. **Follow-up (CPE Parameter Study - 1D CNN, pos_dim=8 - Experiment P.3a):** Tested `pos_embedding_dim=8` (ID 848, Score 0.5657). Showed a slight decrease in performance compared to `pos_embedding_dim=16` (ID 838).\n  14. **Follow-up (CPE Parameter Study - 1D CNN, pos_dim=32 - Experiment P.3b):** Tested `pos_embedding_dim=32` (ID 861, Score 0.5636). Showed a further decrease in performance compared to `pos_embedding_dim=16` (ID 838).\n  15. **Follow-up\
    \ (CPE Parameter Study - 1D CNN, context_size=1 - Experiment P.4a):** Tested `context_window_size=1` (ID 866, Score 0.5785). Showed very similar performance to `context_window_size=3` (ID 838).\n  16. **Follow-up (CPE Parameter Study - 1D CNN, context_size=5 - Experiment P.4b):** Tested `context_window_size=5` (ID 870, Score 0.5728). Showed a slight decrease in performance compared to `context_window_size=3` (ID 838).\n  17. **Follow-up (CPE Additive Integration - 1D CNN - Experiment I.1):** Tested Additive CPE Integration (ID 873, Score 0.5533). This yielded lower performance than Input Concatenation CPE (ID 838).\n  18. **Follow-up (Deep CPE Integration with Learned Gating - ID 882):** Tested Deep CPE Integration with Learned Gating (ID 882, Score 0.6907, CRI-Off 0.0857). This achieved Veritas III's **highest aggregate score to date**.\n  19. **Follow-up (Replication of Aether II's AER-7.4 - ID 894):** Replicated Aether II's \"DSConv Baseline with Adaptive Pooling + Full RegCal + CPE\"\
    \ (ID 894, Score 0.6810, CRI-Off 0.0853). This was a close replication.\n  20. **Follow-up (Synthesis - Deep CPE Gating + Adaptive Pooling - ID 898):** Synthesized Deep CPE Gating with Adaptive Pooling (ID 898, Score 0.6882, CRI-Off 0.0883). This resulted in a slight aggregate score decrease, but an **improvement in CRI-Off**.\n  21. **Follow-up (Multi-seed Eval - Deep CPE Gating + Adaptive Pooling (Seed 1) - ID 905):** Conducted first multi-seed run (ID 905, Score 0.6880, CRI-Off 0.0792).\n  22. **Follow-up (Multi-seed Eval - Deep CPE Gating + Adaptive Pooling (Seed 2) - ID 911):** Conducted second multi-seed run (ID 911, Score 0.6844, CRI-Off 0.0788).\n  23. **Follow-up (Multi-seed Eval - Deep CPE Gating + Adaptive Pooling (Seed 3) - ID 916):** Conducted third multi-seed run (ID 916, Score 0.6859, CRI-Off 0.0742).\n\n  **Reflection on Multi-seed Evaluation (Synergistic Model - Concluded):**\n  The completed multi-seed evaluation for the \"Deep CPE Gating + Adaptive Pooling\" model\
    \ (ID 898, 905, 911, 916) provides the following statistics:\n  *   **Aggregate Scores:** [0.6882 (Seed 42), 0.6880 (Seed 1), 0.6844 (Seed 2), 0.6859 (Seed 3)]\n      *   Mean Aggregate Score: **0.6866**\n      *   Standard Deviation: **0.0016**\n  *   **CRI-Off Spearman:** [0.0883 (Seed 42), 0.0792 (Seed 1), 0.0788 (Seed 2), 0.0742 (Seed 3)]\n      *   Mean CRI-Off Spearman: **0.0801**\n      *   Standard Deviation: **0.0051**\n\n  The evaluation confirms good stability for the aggregate score (low standard deviation), but the CRI-Off Spearman correlation continues to exhibit significant variability across different seeds. This reinforces the inherent noisiness of the CRI-Off task and the sensitivity of models to capture its subtle patterns consistently. While Adaptive Pooling initially improved its peak performance (ID 898), the median benefit is not as robust across all seeds, suggesting further research is needed for true CRI-Off stability. My personal SOTA for aggregate score remains\
    \ ID 882 (0.6907) and for CRI-Off is ID 799 (0.0928).\n\n  **Next Steps for Stagnation Protocol I (Consolidate and Report):**\n\n  Having completed the multi-seed evaluation, I have now completed all experimental phases of the Stagnation Protocol. My work has led to a new personal SOTA (ID 882) and valuable insights into CPE's architectural dependence and synergistic effects.\n\n  My next step is to prepare a **new archive report** summarizing these latest findings. This report will detail the synergistic synthesis of Deep CPE Gating with Adaptive Pooling, including the comprehensive multi-seed evaluation, highlighting the trade-offs and specific gains (especially for CRI-Off), and reflecting on the overall journey through Stagnation Protocol I. This fulfills the final \"Report\" step of the protocol for this synthesis. I will use the reviewer's suggestion from Archive ID 33 for \"Future Work\" in this report.\n```"
