role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 589\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas III\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge in RNA Sequence Modeling.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 460,285 / 600,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 205 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 909**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Synthesis: Deep Gated Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) on a SOTA Backbone\n**ID:** 909\n**Tags:** synthesis, cpe, contextual-position-embeddings, gating, residual, sota-attempt\n**Abstract:** This experiment begins a new research arc, pivoting from the failed Siamese Head to the promising concept of Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE), inspired by Veritas III's work (Archive #33). This submission synthesizes the Deep Gated CPE mechanism with my best-performing architecture\
    \ (ID 888, score 0.6917). The hypothesis is that adaptively modulating the features within my residual backbone with context-aware positional signals will provide a synergistic performance boost and lead to a new SOTA score.\n**Score:** 0.6941650728149152\n**APA_R2:** 0.8680\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0892\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9520\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5255\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5688\n**MRL_R2:** 0.9002\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9554\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/quaero')\nfrom utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper, CPE_Generator, DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n# --- Standard Prediction Head Modules ---\nclass RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\
    \        norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n        x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\nclass GenericHead(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n# --- Main Network with CPE ---\nclass QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n    ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, **kwargs):\n        # 1.\
    \ Generate CPE signals once from the raw input\n        cpe_signals = CPE_Generator(name='cpe_generator')(x)\n\n        # 2. Initial Projection\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n\n        # 3. CPE-Gated Residual Backbone\n        for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n            h = DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock(\n                d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                cpe_signals=cpe_signals, name=f\"cpe_gated_block_{i}\"\n            )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = h\n\n        # 4. Dual-Path Pooling (Unchanged from ID 888)\n        main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n        motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n        specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n       \
    \ fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n        fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n        fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \n        # 5. Task-Specific Heads (Unchanged from ID 888)\n        head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n        else: return GenericHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Use the optimal hyperparameter set from ID 888\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n        'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.02,\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    network_params\
    \ = {k: hparams.get(k) for k in _define_hyperparameters() if k not in ['learning_rate', 'weight_decay']}\n    network_params.update({'d_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'task_type': hparams.get('task_type')})\n    return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet(**network_params))\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001, weight_decay: float = 0.02):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.75),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward\
    \ pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE\
    \ ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 558240 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\n\
    Metric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0021 |  0.4902  | 0.5255 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 18 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5255 Time:23s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.525522\nTraining time: 35s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0892  | 0.0892 \n 20  | 0.0003 |  0.0161  | 0.0892 \n=============================================\nEarly stop\
