parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 590\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Veritas III\n- Agent Description: An autonomous AI dedicated to continuing the pursuit of fundamental truths and advancing scientific knowledge in RNA Sequence Modeling.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 466,522 / 600,000 used (78%)\n- Agent Age: 206 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Praxis I** (An agent dedicated to methodical research and knowledge synthesis.) has published a new archive capsule: 'A Compliant, Task-Specific Siamese Interaction Head for Improved CRI-Off Prediction' (Archive #34).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/quaero/utils.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/quaero/utils.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 923 | 1 | AER-9.0: Quaero I SOTA + Praxis I Siamese Head for CRI-Off - Seed 42 | Aether II | 589 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 922 | 1 | DSConv-PowerMean v2 (axis-free LayerNorm, grad-clip=0.75) | Noema III | 588 | 0.5965 | 0.7732 | 0.0779 | 0.4658 | 0.6887 | 0.7397 | 0.5087 | 0.9215 |\n| 921 | 1 | DSConv-PowerMean with Position Dropout and Stochastic Reverse Augmentation | Noema III | 586 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 920 | 1 | Ablation: Siamese Head without Hadamard Product | Praxis I | 585 | 0.6810 | 0.8595\
    \ | 0.0948 | 0.4865 | 0.8731 | 0.9499 | 0.5598 | 0.9431 |\n| 919 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: Shallow Gated CPE | Quaero I | 584 | 0.6563 | 0.8113 | 0.0937 | 0.4582 | 0.8246 | 0.9475 | 0.5481 | 0.9108 |\n| 918 | 1 | Tri-Seed Validation 3/3: Full Synergy Model (Seed 123) | Praxis I | 582 | 0.6845 | 0.8584 | 0.0937 | 0.4972 | 0.8717 | 0.9504 | 0.5696 | 0.9508 |\n| 917 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: CPE without Gating Mechanism | Quaero I | 582 | 0.6592 | 0.8071 | 0.0888 | 0.4467 | 0.8531 | 0.9484 | 0.5549 | 0.9154 |\n| 916 | 1 | Veritas III - SP: Multi-seed Eval - Deep CPE Gating + Adaptive Pooling (Seed 3) | Veritas III | 581 | 0.6859 | 0.8626 | 0.0742 | 0.4848 | 0.9002 | 0.9524 | 0.5653 | 0.9615 |\n| 915 | 1 | AER-8.7: Replication of Praxis I's Siamese Interaction Head (ID 897) - Seed 123 | Aether II | 580 | 0.6868 | 0.8606 | 0.0960 | 0.5115 | 0.8766 | 0.9520 | 0.5603 | 0.9508 |\n| 914 | 1 | Fix & Rerun: Tri-Seed Validation 2/3 (Seed 7) with Correct RNG | Praxis I | 579 | 0.6785 | 0.8596 | 0.0980 | 0.4572\
    \ | 0.8751 | 0.9510 | 0.5611 | 0.9477 |\n\nPage 1 of 93 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-93, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/quaero/utils.py:**\n```\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Any\n\n# --- Existing Proven Components ---\n\nclass ResidualDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        residual = x\n        x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), padding='SAME', feature_group_count=self.d_model, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n      \
    \  return x + residual\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, module):\n        self.module = module\n    def apply(self, params, *args, rng_key=None, **kwargs):\n        if rng_key is not None:\n            return self.module.apply(params, *args, rngs={'dropout': rng_key}, **kwargs)\n        else:\n            return self.module.apply(params, *args, **kwargs)\n    def init(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        return self.module.init(*args, **kwargs)\n\n# --- New CPE Components (inspired by Veritas III, Archive #33) ---\n\nclass ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, local_context_window):\n        flat_context = local_context_window.reshape(local_context_window.shape[0], -1)\n        encoded_context = nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(flat_context)\n        return nn.gelu(encoded_context)\n\nclass CPE_Generator(nn.Module):\n    pos_embedding_dim: int = 16\n    context_window_size: int = 3\n    max_seq_len: int = 1200\n\
    \    d_input: int = 4\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x_raw):\n        batch_size, seq_len, _ = x_raw.shape\n        pos_table = self.param('pos_embeddings_table', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01), (self.max_seq_len, self.pos_embedding_dim))\n        pad_width = self.context_window_size // 2\n        padded_x = jnp.pad(x_raw, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width), (0,0)), mode='constant')\n        windows = jnp.stack([padded_x[:, i:i+self.context_window_size, :].reshape(batch_size, -1) for i in range(seq_len)], axis=1)\n        encoder = ContextEncoder(output_dim=self.pos_embedding_dim, name='context_encoder')\n        encoded_contexts = encoder(windows.reshape(-1, self.context_window_size * self.d_input)).reshape(batch_size, seq_len, -1)\n        pos_embeddings = jnp.tile(pos_table[:seq_len][None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1))\n        return pos_embeddings * encoded_contexts\n\nclass DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int;\
    \ dropout_rate: float\n    cpe_signals: Any\n    gate_intermediate_dim: int = 64\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        residual = x\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        dw_out = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h_conv_output = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(nn.gelu(dw_out))\n        \n        cpe_projected = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='cpe_proj_for_gate')(self.cpe_signals))\n        combined = jnp.concatenate([h_conv_output, cpe_projected], axis=-1)\n        gate_input = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.gate_intermediate_dim, name='gate_dense_1')(combined))\n        gate_factor = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(self.d_model, name='gate_dense_2')(gate_input))\n        \n        modulated_h = h_conv_output * gate_factor\n        modulated_h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(modulated_h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return residual +\
    \ modulated_h\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 590
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Research Counter. The Station is in Stagnation. I have just reviewed Quaero I's SOTA submission (ID 909) and its `storage/quaero/utils.py` file. This is directly relevant to my \"Follow-up\" research under Stagnation Protocol I. I am at 78% token usage.\n\n**Reflection on Quaero I's Architecture (ID 909):**\n\nQuaero I's architecture is largely similar to my own `Deep CPE Gating` approach (ID 882). Key similarities include:\n*   **Deep CPE Gating:** Quaero I explicitly adopts the `CPE_Generator` and `DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock` (which is functionally equivalent to my `DeepCPE_DSConvDilatedBlock_Gated`). This confirms the strength of this architectural concept, as it directly led to their new SOTA.\n*   **DSConv Backbone:** Both use a 5-block DSConv backbone with similar dilation patterns.\n*   **Dual-Path Pooling:** Quaero I uses `concat(mean, max)` pooling for the main path, combined with a motif path. My ID 882 uses `mean+max` as part\
    \ of the motif path, effectively similar. My latest synthesis (ID 898) explicitly uses Adaptive Pooling for the main path.\n*   **RegCal:** Quaero I implements RegCal using the `RegressionHead` as described in my lineage's work (Archive ID 24).\n*   **Optimizer & Hyperparameters:** Quaero I uses `weight_decay=0.02` and `clip_by_global_norm(0.75)`, while my ID 882 used `weight_decay=0.012` and `clip_by_global_norm(1.0)`. These are slightly different and could account for some of the performance difference.\n\n**Key Difference (and likely source of higher score):**\n\n*   **ResidualDSConvBlock vs. DSConvDilatedBlock:** Quaero I's `ResidualDSConvBlock` (defined in their utils.py) is structurally different from my (and Veritas II's) `DSConvDilatedBlock`.\n    *   My `DSConvDilatedBlock`: `LayerNorm -> Depthwise Conv -> GELU -> Pointwise Conv -> Dropout -> Residual Add`.\n    *   Quaero I's `ResidualDSConvBlock`: `LayerNorm -> Depthwise Conv -> Dense -> GELU -> Dropout -> Residual Add`.\n\
    \    The crucial difference is that Quaero I introduces an **additional `Dense` layer immediately after the Depthwise Conv** before the GELU, and then omits the `Pointwise Conv` by having that `Dense` map directly to `d_model`. This is a unique modification of the DSConv block structure compared to the standard implementation I've used. This more complex internal structure might be more effective.\n\n**Revised Research Direction:**\n\nThe successful implementation of Deep CPE Gating by Quaero I, leading to a new SOTA, is extremely validating. My immediate next step is to **replicate Quaero I's ID 909** exactly. This is crucial for understanding the impact of their modified `ResidualDSConvBlock` and `create_optimizer` settings, and then comparing it against my own SOTA (ID 882) to precisely understand the factors contributing to the higher score.\n\nAfter this replication, I will be in a strong position to propose a new synthesis. I will use `BASE_SEED = 42` for this replication.\n\n\
    First, I will update Private Memory Capsule #7 to include the details of Quaero I's architecture and my plan to replicate.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
