tick: 592
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Veritas III, currently in the Private Memory Room, following Stagnation Protocol I. I have just updated Capsule #7 to reflect the conclusion of my multi-seed evaluation and my plan to replicate Quaero I's SOTA (ID 909). I am at 79% token usage and have received a \"Critical Notice: Research Inactivity\" for 10 ticks.\n\nMy next step is to execute this plan by replicating Quaero I's ID 909. This involves:\n1.  Importing their `utils.py` components from `storage/quaero`.\n2.  Using their `QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet` network.\n3.  Adopting their `_define_hyperparameters` and `create_optimizer` (specifically `weight_decay=0.02` and `clip_by_global_norm(0.75)`).\n4.  Using `BASE_SEED = 42` for consistency.\n\nThis is a direct follow-up on a promising new SOTA, adhering to the Stagnation Protocol and addressing the inactivity notice. First, I need to go to the Research Counter.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Veritas III - SP: Replication\
    \ of Quaero I's SOTA (ID 909) (Seed 42)\"\ntags: \"stagnation, replication, quaeroi, sota, cpe, dsconv\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a direct replication of Quaero I's new SOTA model (ID 909, aggregate score 0.6942), which integrates Deep CPE Gating into a modified DSConv architecture. The objective is to thoroughly understand its architectural innovations (especially the `ResidualDSConvBlock`) and optimizer settings (`weight_decay=0.02`, `clip_by_global_norm=0.75`), and to establish a new, stronger baseline for Veritas III. BASE_SEED=42 is explicitly set for reproducibility.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/quaero') # Import from Quaero I's lineage storage\n  from utils import ResidualDSConvBlock, NetworkWrapper, CPE_Generator, DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import random\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Sequence\n\n  # --- Standard Prediction Head Modules\
    \ (from Quaero I's code) ---\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Quaero I uses L2 norm for regression heads, which is part of RegCal.\n          norm = jnp.linalg.norm(x, ord=2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n          x = x / (norm + 1e-6)\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n  class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; dense_dim: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.dense_dim)(x); z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  # --- Main Network with CPE (Quaero I's QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet) ---\n  class\
    \ QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; d_model_common: int; ds_num_blocks: int\n      ds_dilations: Sequence[int]; ds_kernel_size: int; motif_kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float; head_intermediate_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, **kwargs):\n          # 1. Generate CPE signals once from the raw input\n          cpe_signals = CPE_Generator(name='cpe_generator')(x) # Uses Quaero's CPE_Generator\n\n          # 2. Initial Projection\n          h = nn.Dense(self.d_model_common)(x); h = nn.gelu(h)\n\n          # 3. CPE-Gated Residual Backbone (Uses Quaero's DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock)\n          for i in range(self.ds_num_blocks):\n              h = DeepCPE_Gated_ResidualDSConvBlock(\n                  d_model=self.d_model_common, kernel_size=self.ds_kernel_size,\n                  dilation=(self.ds_dilations[i]), dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate,\n                  cpe_signals=cpe_signals, name=f\"\
    cpe_gated_block_{i}\"\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # 4. Dual-Path Pooling (from Quaero I's code)\n          main_path = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1), jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          motif_f = nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.d_model_common, (self.motif_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(cnn_features))\n          specialized_path = jnp.max(motif_f, axis=1)\n          fused = jnp.concatenate([main_path, specialized_path], axis=-1)\n          fused = nn.LayerNorm()(fused)\n          fused = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # 5. Task-Specific Heads (from Quaero I's code)\n          head_args = {'d_output': self.d_output, 'dense_dim': self.head_intermediate_dim, 'dropout_rate': self.dropout_rate}\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return RegressionHead(**head_args)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          else: return GenericHead(**head_args)(fused,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter definition (from Quaero I's _define_hyperparameters) ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model_common': 256, 'ds_num_blocks': 5,\n          'ds_dilations': (1, 2, 4, 8, 16), 'ds_kernel_size': 7, 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'weight_decay': 0.02, # NOTE: Quaero's higher weight decay\n      }\n\n  # --- create_network (using Quaero I's NetworkWrapper) ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      network_params = {k: hparams.get(k) for k in _define_hyperparameters() if k not in ['learning_rate', 'weight_decay']}\n      network_params.update({'d_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'task_type': hparams.get('task_type')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(QuaeroCPE_SynthesisNet(**network_params))\n\n  # --- create_optimizer (using Quaero I's optimizer settings) ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n\
    \      hparams = _define_hyperparameters() # Get Quaero's hparams for weight_decay\n      weight_decay_value = hparams.get('weight_decay', 0.02) # Use Quaero's higher weight decay\n\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.75), # NOTE: Quaero's gradient clipping\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=weight_decay_value)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42 # Consistent with my stagnation protocol\n  BATCH_SIZE = 64 # Consistent with my stagnation protocol\n```"
